back
Back,Ⓒs.ⒹpfzWaM, pfzWadeSaH; ‘lying on the b(ack)’ uttAnaSayaH; ‘behind oneʼs b(ack)’ parokze-kzaM.<BR>Ⓔadv.Ⓓprati, apA, ni, parA, with verbs; punarnivft 1 A ‘come b(ack)’, ‘give b(ack)’ pratidA 3 U.<BR>Ⓔprep.ⒹSee Before.<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓanumud 1 A, samarT 10, rakz 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (horse), A-aDi-ruh 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 parARud 6 P; See Drive.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]bite,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓparokze aDikzip 6 P, parivad 1 U, asUyati (D.) with dat.; pfzWamAMsaM ad 2 P or KAd 1 P (with gen.).<BR>Ⓝ[Back]biter,Ⓒs.ⒹpiSunaH, pfzWamAMsAdaH, parivAdarataH.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]biting,Ⓒs.ⒹpESunyaM, pari(rI)vAdaH<BR>Ⓝ[Back]bone,Ⓒs.ⒹpfzWavaMSaH, kaSerukA.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]door,Ⓒs.ⒹpakzadvAraM, pakzakaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]gammon,Ⓒs.ⒹcarmapawwikAkrIqA.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]ground,Ⓒs.ⒹpaScAdBUmi f.; ‘throw into the b(ackground)’ (lit.) dfzwipaTAnnivAr 10, niBfte sTA c. (sTApayati); (fig.) ‘Urvaśī throws Lakshmī into the b(ackground)’ urvaSI pratyAdeSaH SriyaH (V. 1); raterapi hrIpadamAdaDAti (K. iii. 57).<BR>Ⓝ[Back]room,Ⓒs.ⒹaMtargfhaM, aMtaH-upa-SAlA.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]side,Ⓒs.ⒹpfzWa-BAgaH-deSaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]slide,Ⓒv. t.ⒹsvaDarmAt BraMS 1 A, 4 P or cyu 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]stairs,Ⓒs.Ⓓupa-pracCannaM-sopAnaM; ‘b(ackstairs) influence’ pracCanna-sAmarTyaM-guRaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]ward,Ⓒa.ⒹparANmuKa (KI f.), atItakAla.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 maMdaDI- mati, maMda, (of a boy).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 anicCu, pratIpa.<BR>Ⓝ[Back]wards,Ⓒadv.ⒹparA, prati, with verbs; pfzWataH, pfzWaBAge-deSe.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 paScAt, pratIpaM; gatAgataM; ‘move b(ackwards) and forward’ gatAgataM-gamanAgamanaM kf 8 U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

