bear
Bear,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓvah 1 P, nI 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 Df 1 P, AlaMb 1 A, Bf 3 U (rAjyaBAramuvAha-baBAra).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 sah 1 A, mfz 4 P, 10, kzam 1 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 prasU 2 A; utpad c., jan c. (janayati); ‘Satyavati bore two sons to the king’ nfpeRa satyavatyAM putrO jAtO-utpAditO, nfpaH satyavatyAM putrAvajIjanat; the same sense ex. in sa nEzaDasya sutAyAM putramutpAdayAmAsa (R. xviii. 1) ‘he had a son by the daughter’ &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 (Cherish) Bf 3 U, Df 1 P; ‘I b(ear) no malice to you’ tavopari dvezaM na DArayAmi, or na tvaM mama dvezapAtraM-sTAnaM; ‘he bore himself bravely on the occasion’ tasminnavasare tena sADu AcaritaM, DIraM vikAMtaM; ‘b(ear) witness’ sAkzyaM dA 3 P [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=30" target="_blank">Page30</a>] (with gen.); ‘b(ear) company’ sahacaraH (rI f.) BU 1 P; ‘b(ear) name’ nAma Bf 3 U, or Df 10; vyapadeSaM Baj 1 A; (evaMvyapadeSaBAjinaH U. 6); ‘b(ear) fruit’ saPalIBU, Pal 1 P; ‘b(ear) in mind’ citte avaDf 10, manasi kf, anusmf 1 P.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹfkzaH, BallUkaH, BAlukaH.<BR>ⓃBorn,Ⓒa.ⒹjAta, utpanna, prasUta, saMBUta; ‘to be b(orn)’ jan 4 A; utpad 4 A; prasU pass., udBU 1 P, saMBU; ‘was b(orn) in the form of a dwarf’ vAmanarUpeRa jAtaH-avatIrRaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear] back,Ⓒv. i.ⒹparA-prati-ni-vft 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear] down,Ⓒv. t.ⒹapAkf 8 U; parAji 1 A, nipat c.; ‘bore down all opposition’ sarvamaMtarAyamapAkurvan.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear] on,Ⓒv. i.ⒹSee Apply.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear] out,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓ(fig.) dfQayati (D.); samarT 10.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear] up,Ⓒv.Ⓓudvah c., uttaMB c., as in Jawiti GawanottaMBitamiva (U. 3).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sah 1 A; ‘b(ear up) under grief’ duHKapratikAraM kuru, SokavaSaM mA gamaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Bear]er,Ⓒs.ⒹvAhaH, haraH, vAhakaH, in comp. vArtAharaH ‘b(earer) of news’<BR>Ⓝ[Bear]ing,Ⓒs.ⒹavasTAnaM, sTiti f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vftti f., vartanaM, AcaraRaM, rIti f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

