Become,Ⓒv. i.ⒹBU 1 P, saMpad 4 A; vft 1 A, jan 4 A; in majority of adjectives ex. by nouns with gam, prAp &c.; ‘became dejected’ vizAdaM gataH, vizaRRo baBUva; ‘b(ecome)s hated’ dvezyatAM yAti; ‘became amazed’ vismayamApede; ‘b(ecom)ing curious’ samupajAtakutUhalaH; ‘what became of the queen Sita’ sItAdevyAH kiM vfttaM (U. 2), kimaBavat.<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓyuj pass., upapad 4 A, (with loc.); gen. ex. by anurUpa, sadfSa (SI f.), ucita, upapanna (all with gen.); ‘does this b(ecome) thy matted hair’ kimidaM jawAnAmanurUpaM, yukta-sadfSaM &c.<BR>Ⓝ[Becom]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓucita, anurUpa, yukta, upapanna; ‘it is b(ecoming)’ sAMprataM.<BR>Ⓝ[Becom]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹyaTocitaM, yaTArhaM, yuktaM, anurUpaM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

