break
Break,Ⓒv. t.ⒹBaMj 7 P (fig. also), KaMq 10.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kzud-piz 7 P, cUrR 10, mfd 9 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 atikram 1 U, 4 P, ullaMG 1 A, 10, aticar 1 P; vilup c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 Bid 7 U, viGaw c. (Gawayati); vidF 9 P, 10, sPuw c. (as heart); ‘b(reak) fast’ pAraRAM nirvft c., prAtarASaM-kalyavartaM sev 1 A; ‘b(reak) wind’ gudaravaM kf 8 U, pard 1 A; ‘b(reak) the way for’ apasf 1 P, apa-i 2 P, apakram.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 vinaS c., ucCid 7 P.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹBid-dF-BaMj- pass., truw 6, 4 P, sPuw 6 P, (sPuwati hfdayaM), dal 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 praBA 2 P; ‘the day broke’ uzAH samAGatA, praBAtA rajanI, dfzwaM dinamuKaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 kzi pass., avasad 1 P, viSF pass., DvaMs 1 A, jf 4, 9 P.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹvicCedaH, nivftti f., virAmaH, BaMgaH; ‘b(reak) of day’ praBAtaM, uzaHkAlaH, aruRodayaH; ‘the story has suffered a b(reak)’ vicCedamApa kaTAprabaMDaH (Ka. 239).<BR>Ⓝ[Break] down,ⒶcUrR 10; (v. i.) See Fail.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] in upon,Ⓐprasahya-sahasA-praviS 6 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] into,ⒶvinI 1 P, dam c. (damayati).<BR>Ⓝ[Break] into (a house),ⒶsaMDiM kftvA praviS.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] loose,Ⓐpramuc, vimuc pass.; ‘the elephant broke loose from the post’ AlAnastaMBaM BaMktvA nirjagAma.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] off,ⒶBaMj, BaMgaM kf 8 U; (v. i.) akasmAt viram 1 P, tyaj 1 P, nivft 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] open,ⒶbalAt-sahasA-udGaw c. or apavf 5 U.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] out,Ⓒ(v. i.)ⒹudDa 1 P, utpad 4 A, prAdurBU, udi 2 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 nirgam 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Break]-through,ⒶnirBaMj, apAnud 6 P, niras 4 P; See Dispel.<BR>Ⓝ[Break]-up,Ⓒ(v. t.)ⒹSee Break (v. i.) ‘the party broke up’ saByAH svaM svaM sTAnaM pratijagmuH.<BR>Ⓝ[Break] upon,ⒶAhan 2 A; ‘the dawn broke upon his eyes’ tasyAkzRoH praBAtamAsIt (S. 2).<BR>Ⓝ[Break] with,Ⓐvivad 1 A, kalahaM kf.<BR>Ⓝ[Break]er,Ⓒs.ⒹBaMjakaH, BedakaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 prastara or tawa-BagnA Urmi f., lahari f.<BR>Ⓝ[Break]fast,Ⓒs.ⒹprAtarASaH, kalyavartaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Break]-water,Ⓒs.ⒹsetuH, DaraRaH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

