care
Care,Ⓒs.ⒹciMtA, OtsukyaM, udvegaH; See Anxiety.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 yatnaH, prayatnaH, AdaraH, manoyogaH; ‘brought up with c(are)’ prayatnasaMvarDitaH, sAdaraM paripAlitaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 sUkzmatA, nipuRatA; ‘searching with c(are)’ nipuRamanvizya; ‘thinking with c(are)’ sunipuRaM vimfSya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 rakzA; avekza; ‘leave under the c(are) of’ See Charge.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 apramAdaH, sAvaDAnatA, avaDAnaM; ‘have a c(are) what you do’ yatkartavyaM tadvimfSya-samIkzya-kuruta.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓava-apa-Ikz 1 A, ciMt 10, mano DA 3 U, oft. ex. by the several nouns above; ‘I do not c(are) now’ aDunAhaM vItaciMtaH, ‘I c(are) very much for your protection’ tava rakzaRe balavAnmamAdaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 gaR 10, (na tfRamapi gaRayati SatruM), Adda 6 A (na tyAgamAdriyate); Ikz 1 A, (the sense being clear), na kAmavfttirvacanIyamIkzate (K. v. 82) ‘a selfwilled person c(are)s not for blame’. ‘take c(are)’ rakz 1 P, ava-Ikz 1 A (SlAGyAM duhitaramavekzasva jAnakIM U. 1), ciMt 10 (tAtastvAM ciMtayizyati).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 lal 10; saMvfD c., pA c. (pAlayati), vinI 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 apramatta-sAvaDAna a. BU 1 P, avaDA 3 U, ‘let c(are) be taken of each character’ pratipAtramADIyatAM yatnaH (S. 1), ‘do not c(are) to think’ sAvaDAnena cetasA na vicArayaMti, iti vicAraM, nAdriyaMte.<BR>Ⓝ[Care]ful,Ⓒa.ⒹAnxious, q. v.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 apramatta, sAvaDAna, aBiyukta, avahita, dakza.<BR>Ⓝ[Care]fully,Ⓒadv.ⒹsAvaDAnaM, prayatnataH, apramattaM, sAdaraM, nipuRaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Care]less,Ⓒa.Ⓓpramatta, anavaDAna, nirapekza, niravaDAna, asamIkzyakArin, ‘to be c(areless) in’ pramad 4 P (with abl.), svADikArAtpramattaH (Me. 1).<BR>Ⓝ[Care]lessly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsapramAdaM, anavaDAnena, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

