Consensus,Ⓒs.ⒹbahujanasaMmati f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consent
Consent,Ⓒv. i.ⒹsaM-anu-man 4 A, anumud 1 A, anujYA 9 U; grah 9 P, svIkf 8 U; See Agree.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹsaMmati f. -taM, anujYA, anumodanaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 matEkyaM, ekacittatA, EkyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 icCA, kAmaH; ‘against oneʼs c(onsent)’ anicCayA, saMmativyatirekeRa, balAt, balena; ‘c(onsent) in writing’ saMmatipatraM; ‘take the c(onsent) of’ anuman c., (BUyopi saKIjanamanumAnayizyAmi S. 3).<BR>Ⓝ[Consent]ient,Ⓒa.Ⓓekamata, ekacitta, saMmata.<BR>Ⓝ[Consent]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsaMmatyA; kAmataH, saMmatipUrvaM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consentaneous
Consentaneous,Ⓒa.ⒹSee Fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consequence
Consequence,Ⓒs.ⒹPalaM, pariRAmaH, udarkaH, uttaraM, uttaraPalaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 gOrava, mahiman m., gurutA, pratizWA, praBAvaH; ‘of no c(onsequence)’ nirarTaka, yatkiMcana.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 sidDi f.; kAryaM, prayojanaM, nimittaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 anumAnaM, UhanaM, aByUhaH; ‘in c(onsequence) of this’ ataH, asmAtkAraRAt, asmAdDetoH, anena hetunA; ‘as a c(onsequence) of thy efforts’ tava yatnasAmarTyAt; ‘immediate c(onsequence)’ sAMdfzwikaM; ‘necessary c(onsequence)’ kAryavaSaH ‘visible c(onsequence)’ dfzwArTaH.<BR>ⓃConsequent,Ⓒa.ⒹAnuzaMgika (kI f.), anuvartin; oft. ex. by PalaM; ‘c(onsequent) upon his coming’ tadAgamanaPalaM.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹanuzaMgaH, PalaM, pariRAmaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Consequent]ial,Ⓒa.ⒹAnuzaMgika, anuvartin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mAnin, sagarva; See Arrogant.<BR>Ⓝ[Consequent]ly,Ⓒadv.Ⓓiti hetoH, ataH, tannimittena, tadanusAreRa; tadarTaM, iti, anena hetunA, asmAtkaraRAt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

conserve
Conserve,Ⓒv. t.ⒹsaMrakz 1 P, pA c. (pAlayati), saMDf 10, gup 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMDA 3 U, upaskf 8 U,<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹmizwaM, modakaH, saMDitaM, upaskaraH, vyaMjanaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Conserv]ation,Ⓒs.ⒹrakzA, saMrakzaRaM, pAlanaM, gupti f., kzemaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Conserv]ative,Ⓒa.ⒹsaMrakzaka, pAlaka.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 navavidvezin, sTitipAlaka.<BR>Ⓝ[Conserv]ator,Ⓒs.ⒹrakzakaH, pAlakaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Conserv]atory,Ⓒs.ⒹrakzAsTAnaM, ADAraH, rakzaRasTAnaM-SAlA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consider
Consider,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓvicar c., vimfS 6 P, A-samA-paryA-loc 10, vi-saM-ciMt 10, samIkz 1 A, (na DarmavfdDezu vayaH samIkzyate K. v. 16); DyE 1 P, saMdfS 1 A, avaDf 10, avekz.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 man 4 A, saMBU c., tark 10, samarT 10, vigaR 10, Akal 10, (sparSamapi pAvanamAkalayaMti Ka. 108)<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 parIkz, nirUp 10, avekz, anusaMDA 3 U, vi-vic 3, 7 U.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 pUj 10, arc 10, man c., pratyupakf; saM pari-tuz c.<BR>Ⓝ[Consider]able,Ⓒa.Ⓓastoka, guru, analpa, pracura, BUri, mahat.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mAnya, Arya, pUjya.<BR>Ⓝ[Consider]ably,Ⓒadv.ⒹatIva, BUri, ati-su- pr., BfSaM, analpaM, atyaMtaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Consider]ate,Ⓒa.ⒹsamIkzya-vimfSya-kArin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kftAvaDAna; Adfta, dattAdara, apramatta, avahita.<BR>Ⓝ[Consider]ately,Ⓒadv.ⒹsamIkzya, vimfSya, avekzayA, apramattaM, avaDAnataH, sAvaDAnaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Consider]ation,Ⓒs.ⒹvicAraH, vicAraRA, AlocanA, vimarSaH, samIkzA, ciMtA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vivecanaM, nirUpaRaM, carcA, parIkzaRaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 AdaraH, apekzA, avekzA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 kAraRaM, nimittaM, hetuH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 gOravaM, gurutA, pratizWA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 pUjA, saMBAvanA, AdaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 pratiPalaM, pAritozikaM; ‘in c(onsideration) of’ apekzayA in comp., samIkzya, Alocya, vicArya, praTamamiti prekzya BagavatEkoparADo marzayitavyaH (S. 4) ‘in c(onsideration) of its being the first’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consign
Consign,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓnikzip 6 P, nyas 4 U, dA 3 U, 1 P, f c. (arpayati), pratipad c., ‘c(onsign) to the flames’ agnisAtkf 8 U.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 upa-pra-vini-yuj 7 A, 10.<BR>Ⓝ[Consign]ment,Ⓒs.ⒹarpaRaM, nyasanaM, pratipAdanaM<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

consist
Consist,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓ(of, in) Ex. by rUpa, Atmaka, maya (yI f.) in comp.; ‘Ojas c(onsist)s in abundance of compounds’ samAsaBUyastvarUpaM-stvaM nAma ojaH; ‘bodyʼs ornament c(onsist)s in true knowledge’ satyajYAnAtmakaM SarIraBUzaRaM; See Compose.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMvft 1 A, saMsTA-saMBU 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Consist]ence,Ⓒs.ⒹGanatA, sAMdratA, SyAnatA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sTiratA, dfQatA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 aviroDaH, AnurUpyaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Consist]ency,Ⓒs.ⒹsaMgatatA, saMvAdaH, aviroDaH, AnurUpyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sTiratA, acApalyaM<BR>Ⓝ[Consist]ent,Ⓒa.ⒹavirudDa, sadfSa (SI f.), yogya, anurUpa, saMvAdin; ‘his conduct is c(onsistent) with his words’ tasyAcaraRaM (karma) vacasA na vivadate, vacaso na virudDaM, vacasA na visaMvadati; ‘inc(onsistent)’ visaMvAdin, virudDa; (parArTamudyamaBftaH) svArTAviroDena (Bh. i. 74) ‘c(onsistent)ly with their own interests’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sTira, acapala, alola.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 dfQa, Gana, sAMdra, SyAna.<BR>Ⓝ[Consist]ently,Ⓒadv.ⒹavirudDaM, aviroDena, anusArataH.<BR>Ⓝ[Consist]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹEx. by maya (yI f.), Atmaka (AtmikA f.) in comp.; ‘c(onsisting) for the most part’ ex. by BUyizWa affixed; ‘assembly c(onsisting) of learned men’ aBirUpaBUyizWA parizad (S. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

