contend
Contend,Ⓒv. i.ⒹsaMyat 1 A, vigrah 9 P, kalahAyate (D.), viruD 7 U, pratikf 8 U, vivad 1 A, yuD 4 A, sparD 1 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vAgyudDaM kf, pratyavasTA 1 A, (atrApare pratyavatizWaMte S. B. 57).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 yat-cezw 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Contend]er,Ⓒs.ⒹvipakzaH, pratiyodDf m., vivAdin m., pratiyogin m., pratipakzaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Contend]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹviroDin; vivadamAna, kalahaSIla.<BR>ⓃContention,Ⓒs.ⒹvivAdaH, vigrahaH, kalahaH, kaliH, vipratipatti f., vAgyudDa, vipralApaH; ‘point (bone) of c(ontention)’ vivAda-vizayaH-vastu n.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMGarzaH, sparDA.<BR>ⓃContentious,Ⓒa.Ⓓkalahapriya, vivAdin, viroDin, kalaha-vivAda-SIla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

content
Content,Ⓒa.ⒹsaM-, pari-, tuzwa, tfpta, niHspfha, vitfzRa, prIta, praSAMta, hfzwa; ‘to be c(ontent)’ tuz 4 P, tfp 4 P, saMpari-°; ‘is c(ontent) with even little’ svalpakenApi tuzyati; ‘poor and c(ontent) is rich and rich enough’ saMtoza eva puruzasya paraM niDAnaM.<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓtuz c., tfp c., saM-pari-°, naMd c., prI 9 P; ‘c(ontent)s the eyes’ kftArTayati cakzuH.<BR>Ⓝ[Content]ment,Ⓒs.ⒹsaM-pari-tozaH, tfpti f., prIti f., aspfhA, vitfzRA, Dfti f., kAma, nivftti f.; ‘water to the heartʼs c(ontentment)’ prakAmajalaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (‘c(ontent)s’) GanaPalaM (golasya); pUrakaM, aMtarmataM; ‘c(ontent)s of a letter’ leKArTaH; ‘if so, I shall know its c(ontent)s’ tena hyasya gfhItArTA BavAmi (V. 2); ‘table of c(ontent)s’ sUcIpatraM, anukramaRikA.<BR>Ⓝ[Content]ed,Ⓒa.Ⓓtuzwa, tfpta, prIta, &c.; ‘keep c(ontented)’ anuraMj c., prI 9 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Content]edly,Ⓒadv.ⒹprItyA, saMtozeRa, tuzwyA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

