down
Down,Ⓒs.Ⓓkomalaroman n.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 tUlaM, komalapakzaH; ‘d(own) of goose’ haMsatUlaM; tfRaloman n. (of plants).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 nirvanaparvataH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 nimnaM, nimnapradeSaH; ‘the road having ups and d(own)s’ natonnataBUmiBAgo mArgaH; ‘ups and d(own)s’ pAtotpAtAH; ‘there are ups and d(own)s in our condition (in life) as in the course of the wheel’ nIcErgacCatyupari ca daSA cakranemikrameRa (Me. 112).<BR>Ⓔprep.ⒹaDaH, aDastAt (with gen.); gen. ex. by anu in comp.; ‘d(own) the current’ anurayaM; ‘d(own) to’ yAvat (with acc.), paryaMtaM in comp.; ‘d(own) to the present day’ adya yAvat.<BR>Ⓔadv.ⒹaDaH, aDastAt, nIcEH, nIce; gen. ex. by ava-ni-aDaH pr. to roots; ‘bent d(own)’ avanata, nIcEH praRata; ‘to come d(own)’ ava-ni-pat 1 P; ‘d(own) with the tyrant’ nipAtyatAM-ucCedyatAM-asO prajApIqakaH; ‘d(own)cast’ aDomuKa (KI f.), avanatadfzwi, vizaRRa, aDodfzwi, dInavadana, mlAna, Kinna; ‘d(own)-fall’ vini-apa-pAtaH, vinASaH, kzayaH, ucCedaH, viDvaMsaH, layaH; ‘d(own)-hearted’ Kinna-dIna-cetas, mlAna, vizaRRa; ‘d(own)-hill’ pravaRaBUmi f., upatyakA; ‘d(own) lying’ prAptaprasavakAlA; (s.) SayanasamayaH; ‘d(own) right’ avakra, akuwila, spazwa, suvyakta, asaMdigDa, pratyakza; (adv.) avakraM, akuwilaM, saralaM, aDoDaH; vyaktaM, pratyakzaM, suspazwaM, BinnArTaM, sarvataH, sAkalyena, su-ati pr.<BR>Ⓝ[Down]ward,Ⓒa.ⒹpravaRa, patanaSIla, aDastana (nI f.), aDogAmin, patayAlu, pAtuka.<BR>Ⓔadv.Ⓓ(downwards) ava pr., aDaH, avAk, aDastAt.<BR>Ⓝ[Down]y,Ⓒa.Ⓓmfdulomavat.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mfdu, komala, sukumAra, suKasparSa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

