fall
Fall,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓcyu 1 A, gal 1 P, sraMs 1 A, pat 1 P, ni-ava°, BraMS 1 A, 4 P; ‘fell under his displeasure’ tasyAkfpApAtraM-kopAspadaM-baBUva.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mf 6 A, naS 4 P, vi-pra-DvaMs 1 A, pra-lI 4 A, prAREH viyuj pass.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 avasad 1 P, kzi-apaci pass., nyUnIBU 1 P, hras 1 P; ‘a cow f(all)s beneath his paw’ gOstasya naKapaMjare patati, naKarAkrAMtA Bavati; ‘when the wind fell’ SAMte pavane.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 dru 1 P, praviS 6 P, avatF 1 P, (gaMgA sAgaraM praviSati-avatarati); ‘f(all) foul of’ saMGaww 1 A, Akram 1 U, 4 P; vi-vad 1 A; ‘f(all) to the ground’ DvaMs, (DvaMsitaste utsAha-vfttAMtaH S. 2), vinaS.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹpAtaH, patanaM, cyuti f.; DvaMsaH, BraMSaH, sraMsanaM, aDaH-ni-patanaM, ava-ni-pAtaH; ‘in rapid f(all) descend’ javena nipataMti.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sTAnaBraMSaH-cyutiH, apakarzaH, padanASaH-BraMSaH-cyutiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 pra-vi-DvaMsaH, saM-upa-pari-kzayaH, avasAdaH; ‘rise and f(all)’ pAto-tpAtAH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 hrAsaH, apacayaH, nyUnIBAvaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 nirJaraH, prasravaRaM; prapAtaH, vAripravAhaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 pAtuka-pravaRa-BUmi f.; ‘f(all) of snow’ tuzAravarzaH, himasruti f.; ‘f(all) of rain’ DArAsaMpAtaH, DArAsAraH, AsAraH.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] away,ⒶmlE-glE 1 P, nirgal, pra-lI, naS.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 svaDarmAd BraMS or cyu.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] back,ⒶparAvft 1 A, apa-sf-sfp 1 P, avasTA 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] in with,ⒶsaMman 4 A, aByupa-gam 1 P; See Agree.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 Asad c., sa-hasA dfS 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] into,Ⓐni-aMtaH-pat; ‘f(all) into vice’ durmArgagAmino BavaMti; ‘f(all) into misfortune’ vipadgrastA BavaMti<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] off,Ⓐcyu BraMS.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 apasf 1 P, palAy 1 A, viyuj pass.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 svaDarmaM tyaj 1 P, pat.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 hrAsaM gam 1 P, kzi-apaci-saMhf- pass., hras.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] on, [Fall] upon,ⒶAkram, aBidru^1, Apat, avaskaMd 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] out,Ⓐvivad 1 A, viprati-pad 4 A, kalahaM kf 8 U.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] short,ⒶnyUnIBU, hras, kzi-saMhf pass.; ‘his arrow fell short of its aim’ sa lakzyacyutasAyakoBUt; ‘words f(all) short in describing your greatness’ tava mahimAnamutkIrtya vacaH saMhriyate (R. x. 32).<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] to,Ⓐpra-upa-kram 1 A, prAraB 1 A; ‘they fell to blows’ parasparaprahAramAreBire.<BR>Ⓝ[Fall] under,Ⓐ(power) vaSaM i 2 P, a-DIna a. BU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aMtarBU, aMtargaR pass.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

