hand
Hand,Ⓒs.ⒹhastaH, pARiH, karaH, SayaH, paMcaSAKaH, BujAdalaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pArSvaH, BAgaH, pakzaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 karaRaM, viDAnaM, cezwA, kriyA, vyApAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 vaSaH-SaM, aDikAraH, Sakti f., praButvaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 kartf m., kAraH-kArakaH in comp.; karmakaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 pradeSinI, sUcinI; kIlaH; sUci f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 lipi f., libi f., akzarasaMsTAnaM, liKitaM; ‘h(and) to hand’ hastA-hasti, bAhUbAhavi, muzwImuzwi; ‘h(and) to h(and) fight’ niyudDaM, bAhuyudDaM; ‘on the one h(and)-on the other h(and)’ ekataH-anyataH, itaH-itaH, ekaMca-apa-raMca; oft. by ca-ca; ‘on the other h(and)’ viparyaye, pratyuta, tu, tAvat; ‘if on the other h(and)’ aTa, yadi; ‘on all h(and)s’ sarvaTA, sarvatra; ‘at h(and)’ pratyAsanna, samIpavartin, Asanna, saM-nihita, samIpaM-pe; ‘in h(and)’ haste, hastagata, hastavartin, karatalagata; ‘subject in h(and)’ prakftaM, prastutaM; ‘h(and) in h(and)’ ekatra, samavAyasaMbaM-Dena; saha, sahitaM, samaM, saMBUya; ‘to give a helping h(and)’ hastAvalaMbaM dA 3 U; ‘given a helping h(and)’ dattahastAvalaMba, ‘living from h(and) to mouth’ utpannaBojin; durgata, kfcCra-gata; ‘on h(and)’ anupayukta, avyApfta; (of books &c.) avikrIta; ‘sword in h(and)’ Kaqgahasta, kfpARapARi; ‘off-h(and)’ ASu, avicArya, avilaMbaM; Akasmika-pratyutpanna-aciMtita-pUrva a.; ‘out of h(and)’ sapadi, tatkzaRAt; ‘to take in h(and)’ AraB 1 A, prastu 2 U, upakram 1 A; ‘lend a h(and)’ upakf 8 U, anugrah 9 P, sAhAyyaM kf; ‘lay h(and)s on’ Df 1 P, grah, ADfz c., parAmfS-spfS 6 P, ‘to have a h(and) in’ sahakArin a. BU, sahAyaH BU; ‘have or get the upper h(and)’ aBi-BU, pra-BU, atiric pass.; ‘under-h(and)’ niMdya, Calena, sakapawa; ‘clap the h(and)s’ karatAlaM vad c.; ‘to support with the h(and)’ kareRa ava-A-laMb 1 A, ha-stAvalaMbaM dA; ‘the open or extended h(and)’ capewaH, carpawaH, prahastaH, pratalaH; ‘hollow of the h(and)’ karapuwaM, hastakozaH; ‘two open h(and)s joined together’ saMhatatalaH, pratalaH; ‘folded h(and)’ prasftiH; ‘folded h(and)s joined’ aMjaliH; ‘clenched h(and)’ muzwi m. f.; ‘h(and) with the fist clenched’ ratniH.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓhaste-kare-nikzip 6 P or dA 3 U or f c. (arpayati); ‘h(and) down’ paraMparayA-krameRa-saMcar c. or saMkram c.; ‘to be h(and)ed down’ paraMparayA Agam 1 P; upa-, saMkram 1 U, 4 P, (yAni BagavataHkfSASvAtkOSika-mfzimupasaMkrAMtAni U. 1); (in sacred texts) A-samA-mnA pass.; ‘h(and)book’ hastaneyaM pustakaM; laGugraMTaH; ‘h(and)cuff’ hastapASaH-nigaqaH, karabaMDanaM; (v. t.) pASena hastO baMD 9 P or saMyam 1 P or yaMtr 10; ‘h(and)-kerchief’ karavastraM; ‘h(and)-maid’ cewI, dAsI, paricArikA; ‘h(and) mill’ hastacAlitA pezaRI; ‘h(and)-weapon’ hastA-yuDaM, karaSastraM; ‘h(and)-writing’ liKitaM, lipi-bi f., akzarasaMsTAnaM; ‘oneʼs own h(and)-writing’ hastaleKaH, svahastAkzaraM.<BR>Ⓝ[Hand]ful,Ⓒs.Ⓓmuzwi m. f.; ‘a h(andful) of grass’ tfRamuzwiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 alpa-stoka-saMKyA, oft. by alpa-stoka a.<BR>ⓃHandicraft,Ⓒs.ⒹSilpaM, hastalAGavaM, hasta-SilpaM-karman n. SilpavidyA; ‘h(andicraft)s-man’ Si-lpin m., SilpakAraH, karmakaraH.<BR>ⓃHandiwork,Ⓒs.ⒹhastakftaM karma.<BR>ⓃHandy,Ⓒa.Ⓓdakza, laGuhasta, karadakza, suprayogavat, kuSala, nipuRa, catura, pawu, kziprakArin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 suKaneya, laGuBAra, adurvaha.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 Asanna, nikawa, pratyutpanna.<BR>Ⓝ[Handi]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹhastalAGavena, dakzatayA, sapAwavaM, yuktyA, caturaM, dAkzyeRa.<BR>Ⓝ[Handy]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹdakzatA, hastalAGavaM, karadakzatA, kOSalaM, cAturyaM, nEpuRyaM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

