high
High,Ⓒa.Ⓓucca, unnata, ucCrita, samucCrita, socCrAya, tuMga, prAMSu, udagra, uttuMga, udgata, unnamra, UrDva.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 uttama, viSizwa, muKya, SrezWa, parama, agrya, mahA-praDAna- in comp.; See Principal.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 pracaMqa, tIkzRa, tIvra, balavat, tarasvin, prabala; See Strong.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 udAtta, uttAla; ‘a h(igh) tone’ udAttaH, ucca-tAra-svaraH, tAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 (‘Of h(igh) rank’) viSizwa, utkfzwa, utkfzwa-viSizwa-padasTa, uttama-parama-padaBAj, labDapratizWa, pratipattimat, sagOrava.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 (‘Of h(igh) family’) kulIna, mahAkula, aBijAta, aBijanavat, kulaja, mahAkulaprasUta.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 garvodData, darpADmAta, sAvalepa, garvita, avalipta, utsikta.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 gahana; ‘h(igh) water’ pra-vfdDA velA; ‘it is h(igh) noon’ (naBasaH) maDyamalaMkaroti BAnuH; ‘h(igh) and low’ uccAvaca, aDarottara, uttamADama, unnatAnata, natonnata, nimnonnata; ‘h(igh)er and h(igh)er’ aDikADikaM, uttarottaraM; ‘h(igh) price’ mahAmUlya; ‘h(igh) ground’ unnataBUH; ‘as h(igh) as’ mAtra (trI f.) dva-yasa (sI f.), daGna (GnI f.) in comp.; ‘he has a h(igh) opinion of you’ sa tvAM bahu ma-nyate.<BR>Ⓔadv.ⒹuccEH, uccaM, ati-su pr.; UrDvaM, upari, uttamaM, paramaM; ‘on h(igh)’ UrDvaM, upari; ‘from on h(igh)’ uparizwAt; ‘the sea runs h(igh)’ balavatkzubDaH sAgaraH. ‘H(igh)-birth’ kulInatA, kulotkarzaH, ABijAtyaM; ‘h(igh)-blest’ atipuRyavat, mahABAga, atiDanya, paramasuKaBAj; ‘h(igh)-blown’ atyucCUna, ati-sPIta; ‘h(igh)-born’ kulIna, mahAkula-jAta-prasUta, aBijAta, sujAta, aBijanavat, sadvaMSya, SrezWa-uttama-kulodBava; ‘h(igh)-bred’ kulIna, SizwAcAra, sujana, suSIla, sadBAvaviSizwa, sOjanyopeta, sadAcAra, sADuvftta; ‘h(igh)-built’ socCrAya, ucca; ‘h(igh)-day’ utsavadinaM, udDarza-divasaH; ‘h(igh)-fed’ atipuzwa, hfzwapuzwa; ‘h(igh)-flying’ aparimita; ‘h(igh)-hand’ OdDatyaM, garvaH, uddAmatvaM; niryaMtraRatvaM; ‘h(igh)-handed’ udData, sagarva, uddAma, aniyaMtraRa, ucCfMKala, svErin; ‘h(igh)-hung’ UrDvabadDa; ‘h(igh)-land’ aDityakA, unnataBUmi f.; (a.) parvatIya, unnataH ‘h(igh)-lander’ parvatIyaH, parvatavAsin m.; ‘h(igh)-mettled’ mahAsattva, urusattva, ojasvin, adInacitta, tejasvin; garvita, atimadAnvita; ‘h(igh)-minded’ mahA-tman, mahAmanaska, udAra-DI-cetas-carita, mahecCa, mahASaya; ‘h(igh)-principled’ sADu-caritra, puRyAtman, puRyaSIla; ‘h(igh)-priest’ purohitADyakzaH; ‘h(igh)-prized’ mahAmUlya, mahArGa, bahumata; ‘h(igh)-red’ GanAruRa, atirakta; ‘h(igh)-road, -street, -way’ rAjamArgaH-paTaH, mahApaTaH-mArgaH, GaMwApaTaH, saMsaraRaM, raTyA, vi-SiKA, pratolI; ‘h(igh)-seasoned’ suvAsita; ‘h(igh)-spirited’ mahA-uru-sattva, adInavftti, ojasvin, Urjita, mahecCa; ‘a h(igh)-spirited speech’, UrjitASrayaM vacanaM (Ki. ii. 1); ‘h(igh)-treason’ rAjadrohaH, rAjApaTyakAritvaM; ‘h(igh)-wrought’ yatna-saMskfta, prayatnaparizkfta; ‘h(igh)-wayman’ paripaMTin m., dasyuH, vAwa-pAwaccaraH, pAdavikaGnaH.<BR>Ⓝ[High]est,Ⓒa.ⒹuccEstama, tuMgatama, uttama, parama.<BR>Ⓝ[High]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹuccaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 BfSaM, atyaMtaM, nitAMtaM, paramaM, paraM, atIva, ati-su pr.; See Exceedingly, ‘h(ighly)-pleased’ paramAnaMdaM-BAj, harzakAzWAM gata.<BR>Ⓝ[High]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹdevaH (vI f.), atra-tatra-Bavat (tI f.).<BR>ⓃHeight,Ⓒs.ⒹucCrAyaH, ucCrayaH, utseDaH, ArohaH, unnayaH, tuMgatA, uccatA; utkarzaH, unnati f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 uccasTAnaM; utseDaH, unnataBUBAgaH, giriH, parvataH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 SiKaraM, agraM, SfMgaM, SiKA, cUqA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 (parA) kAzWA, kowiH; atiBUmiH; paramAvaDiH, utta-mAvaDiH; ‘being in the h(eight) of joy’ AnaMda-kowimaDigata.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 kulotkarzaH, parmapadaM, SrezWatvaM, viSizwatA; ‘the h(eight) of winter’ Si-SiramaDyaM, kaWorIBUtaH SiSiraH.<BR>Ⓝ[Height]en,Ⓒv. t.ⒹunnI 1 P, utkfz 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vfD c., upaci 5 U, Svi c., sPAy c. (sPAvayati); See Add to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

