hold
Hold,Ⓒv. t.ⒹDf 1 P, 10, avalaMb 1 A, A-dA 3 A, grah 9 U, parAmfS 6 P, hastena Df or avalaMb.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 staMB 9 P, ni-ava-ruD 7 U, balAd Df.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (possess) Bf 3 U, A-DA 3 U; See Have.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 (Contain) Df, parigraha, A-DA, samAviS c., Bf, A-dA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 pA c. (pAlayati), rakz 1 P, na tyaj 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 (As a festival) anuzWA 1 P, sev 1 A, pA c. (pAlayati), kf 8 U, saM-pad c., nirvah c., vi-DA, yaTAviDi kf, aBinaMd c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 man 4 A, gaR 10; See Consider, ‘I h(old) them of no account’ kA-kiyatI-mAtrA tezAM matpurataH, tAnahaM tfRAya manye or tfRI-karomi; ‘h(old) an opinion’ mataM avalaMb or ASri 1 U, man; ‘h(old) oneʼs tongue’ jihvAM Df or rakz; ‘h(old) your tongue’ vAcaMyamo Bava, vAcaM niyacCa, tUzRIM-jozaM-Assva; ‘h(old) a meeting’ saBAM mil c. or samA-hve 1 P; ‘a meeting was held’ parizad militA; ‘h(old) in esteem’ bahu man; ‘h(old) in contempt’ avagaR, avaman, tfRIkf, tfRAya man; ‘h(old) a council’ saBAM nimaMtr 10 A or Ahve; ‘h(old) a consultation’ saMmaMtr, maMtraRAM kf; ‘I h(old) you responsible for this act’ asya tvayottaraM dAtavyaM.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹsTA 1 P, sTirIBU, saMsTA 1 A; cirasTA-yIBU sTAyIBU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anubaMD 9 P or pass.; saM-saMj pass., saMlagnIBU, AlaMb 1 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 viram 1 P, nivft 1 A (with abl.); AtmAnaM saMyam 1 A or nigrah, parihf 1 P, tyaj; ‘hold hold!’ virama virama, mA mA, evaM, mA tAvat-.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 aDIna a. BU, ASri, ava-A-laMb.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 (As a rule) gam, na vyaBicar 1 P; ‘this rule h(old)s everywhere’ sarvagAmI-avyaBicArI-ayaM niyamaH.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹDaraRaM, Dfti f., grahaH-haRaM, avalaMbaH-banaM, hastena grahaRaM-DaraRaM, ‘letting go the h(old)’ mukta-srasta-hasta, muktagraha.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kArA, kArAgfhaM; kArAgAraM, baMDanasTAnaM, gupti f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 ADAraH, A-ava-laMbaH-banaM, upastaMBaH, ASrayaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 durgaM, kowaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 muzwi m. f., vAraMgaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 AspadaM, padaM, aDikAraH, vaSaH-SaM; ‘red colour takes a firm h(old) on a white cloth’ rAgaH Suklapawe sTAyIBavati (P. i. 1); ‘had a h(old) on the mind of the people’ sa lokasya mana Adade (R. iv. 8); ‘the advice took no h(old) on (her) mind’ leBeMtaraM cetasi nopadeSaH (R. vi. 66).<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] back,Ⓐni-vf c., vAr 10, saMhf 1 P, nigrah, vikxp 1 A, vicar c.; See Hesitate.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] forth,ⒶdfS c., puro niDA.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] in,Ⓐnigrah, pratisaMhf, ni-saM-yam.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] off,ⒶvilaMb 1 A, vikxp.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] on,Ⓐpravft c., na viram, na muc 6 P, na tyaj, udvah 1 P, nirvah c.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] out,Ⓐprasf c., vitan 8 U, dIrGIkf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 dfS c., upanyas 4 U, upakzip 6 P, upasTA c. (sTApayati); (v. i.) ciraM yAvatsah 1 A or yuD 4 A or pratikf.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] together,ⒶsaMbaMD pass., saMSliz 4 P, saMlag 1 P<BR>Ⓝ[Hold] up,Ⓐunnam c. (namayati), udyam, AcCri. 1 U or c., UrDvIkf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 uttaMB, avazwaMB, A-ava-laMb, Bf, Df.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold]er,Ⓒs.ⒹDArakaH, DAra-yitf m., grAhakaH, DaraH-ADAraH- in comp.<BR>Ⓝ[Hold]ing,Ⓒs.ⒹDaraRaM, grahaRaM, &c.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹDArin, Dara in comp.; oft. by hasta in comp.; ‘h(olding) a sword’ kfpARapARiH.<BR>ⓃHoldfast,Ⓒs.ⒹgrAhakaH, grahaRI, baMDanI, kuqupaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 dfQa-badDa-muzwiH, amuktahastaH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

