ill
Ill,Ⓒa.Ⓓduzwa, pApa, asat, asADu, garhya, Kala, kutsita, aBadra, amaMgala, aSuBa, gen. ex. by dur, ku, apa, vi, kad, pr.; See Ban; oft. by a in comp.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 asvasTa, asvasTa-asusTa-SarIra, asusTa, asusTita, vyADita, sAmaya, rogin; gen. ex. by Arta, grasta, Atura, pIqita in comp.; ‘i(ll) with fever’ jva-rArta, jvarapIqita.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹduzwatA, KalatA, asADutA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pApaM, durAcAraH, aDarmaH, durvfttaM, dozaH, aparADaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 anizwaM, aSuBaM, amaMgalaM, akuSalaM, aBadraM, duHKaM, durgati f., Apad-vipad f., vyasanaM, utpAtaH, anarTaH, arizwaM, anizwapAtaH, kazwaH-zwaM, apAyaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 apakAraH, apakfti f., ahitaM, apAyaH, kzati-hAni f., kzayaH, apa-cayaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 rogaH, vyADiH, AmayaH, pIqA, upatApaH, asvAsTyaM; See Disease.<BR>Ⓔadv.ⒹasADu, anAryaM, asamyak, duzwaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 duHKena, kazwena, kfcCreRa; in comp. words, ex. by dur, ku, apa, vi, kad, a, duzwa, pApa; ‘i(ll)-advised’ aparIkzita, avimfSya kfta; ‘i(ll)-affected’ vi-apa-rakta, drohabudDi, ahitEzin; ‘i(ll)-arranged, -ordered, -regulated’ duzkrama, durviracita, avyatasTitaH ‘i(ll)-behaved, -bred, -natured’ avinIta, duHSIla, durvftta, kuSIla, avinaya, durvinIta, aSizwa, asamya, durAcAra, pApa, kuvftti, vinayApeta; ‘i(ll)-breeding’ avinayaH, duHSIlatA, asaByatA, vinayapramATaH, durvftti f., durAcAraH; ‘i(ll)-conditioned’ durgata, duH-sTita; ‘i(ll)-dressed’ durvAsas, kuprAvfta; ‘i(ll)-fame’ ayaSaH, apakIrti f., apratizWA; ‘i(ll)-fated’ durBAgya, maMdaBAgya, durdEva, dEvopa-hata, durdEvagrasta-upahata; ‘i(ll)-favoured, -formed, -shaped’ apa-ku-rUpa, kadAkAra, durdarSana; ‘i(ll)-fitted’ ayogya, anarha, anucita; ‘i(ll)-gotten’ anyAyArjita; ‘i(ll)-grounded’ amUlaka; ‘i(ll)-judged’ avimfSya-avicArya-kfta, anAlocita; ‘i(ll)-judging’ vivekaSUnya; nirviveka; ‘i(ll)-looking’ durdarSana, kurUpa; ‘i(ll)-luck’ durdEvaM, durBAgyaM, maMdaBAgyaM, dEvaviparyAsaH-durvipAkaH, durjAtaM, anizwaM; See (s.); ‘i(ll)-nature, -temper’ duH-SIlaM, duzprakfti f., vakraBAvaH-SIlaM, vAma-SIlaM, BAvapratIpatA, vAmaSIlatA,