know
Know,Ⓒv. t.ⒹjYA 9 U, vid 2 P, buD 1 P, avagam 1 P, ava-i 2 P, aBijYA, paricita a. BU 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anu-BU, vi-BU c., upalaB 1 A, grah 9 U; ‘how should a dependent k(now) of sincere happiness (pleasure)’ parAyattaH prIteH kaTamiva rasaM vettu puruzaH (Mu. 3).<BR>Ⓝ[Know]er,Ⓒs.ⒹjYatf m., jYAnin m., vetf m. jYaH-aBijYaH in comp.<BR>Ⓝ[Know]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹvijYa, jYAnin; gen. ex. by vid, jYa or aBijYa in comp.; ‘k(nowing) Dharma’ Darmavid, DarmajYaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Know]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹjYAnapUrvaM, kAmataH, boDa-mati-budDi-pUrvaM, jAnat a. with api.<BR>Ⓝ[Know]ledge,Ⓒs.Ⓓ(Act) jYAnaM, pari-vi-jYAnaM, boDaH-DanaM, vedanaM, avagamaH, upalaMBaH, upalabDi f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Learning) jYAnaM, vidyA, vidvattA, pAMqityaM, vyutpannatA, vEduzyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 aBijYAnaM, paricayaH; ‘spiritual k(nowledge)’ AtmajYAnaM-vidyA, paramArTajYAnaM, aDyAtmavidyA, paramArTaH, brahmavidyA, paramArTaboDaH; ‘acquiring k(nowledge)’ vidyArjanaM, vidyAgamaH, jYAnaprApti f.; ‘eager after k(nowledge)’ jYAnecCu, jijYAsu; ‘thirst after k(nowledge)’ jijYA-sA, jYAnalipsA, jYAnecCA; ‘according to oneʼs k(nowledge)’ yaTAjYAnaM; ‘for the right k(nowledge) of words and their meaning’ vAgarTapratipattaye (R. i. 1); ‘without the k(nowledge) of’ avijYApya, anivedya, agocaraM-reRa, parokzaM-kze; ‘with the k(nowledge) of’ gocaraM-reRa, pratyakzaM, sAkzAt, samakzaM; ‘to come to the k(nowledge) of’ Sruti-karRa-paTaM yA-i- 2 P or gam 1 P; ‘k(nowledge) is power’ budDiryasya balaM tasya (P. i. 8).<BR>ⓃKnown,Ⓒa.ⒹjYAta, vidita, avagata, boDita, upalabDa, anuBUta, viBAvita.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 KyAta, vi-Sruta, prasidDa, vi-pra-KyAta, vijYAta; ‘to make k(nown)’ vi-jYA c. (jYApayati), ni-A-vid c., buD c., ‘to become k(nown)’ jYA-prati-i pass.; ‘be it k(nowledge) to your honor’ eva-matraBavaMto vidAMkurvaMtu; ‘be it k(nown)’ jYAtaM-viditaM-astu; ‘became k(nowledge) by that name’ tadAKyayA (Buvi) papraTe (R. xv. 101), tadA-KyAM jagAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="