Lead,Ⓒs.ⒹsIsaM, sIsakaM, nAgaM, yogezwaM, vapraM; ‘red l(ead)’ siMdUraM, nAgasaMBavaM, raktacUrRaM, nAgajaM, nAgagarBaM.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹnAyakatvaM, netftvaM, aDizWAtftvaM, muKyatvaM, agragamanaM-yAnaM, puraHsaraRaM.<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹnI 1 P, vah 1 P, prAp c., gam c. (gamayati) (all with two accusatives); A-dA 3 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Way) dfS c., A-nir-diS 6 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 aDi-zWA 1 P, aDyAs 2 A, praRI, A-nir-diS; puraskf 8 U, agraRIH-nAyakaH-agresaraH-BU 1 P (with gen.); vasizWADizWitA devyaH (U. 1) ‘led by Vasishtha’ &c., daSaraTasya dArAnaDi-zWAya (U. 4) ‘led by the demon’ dAnavaM puraskftya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 Akfz 1 P, pra-vi-luB c., pra-vft c. prer c., protsah c. nI; mUQaH parapratyaya-neyabudDiH (M. 1) ‘has his mind led by the convictions of others’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 (Time) nI, gam c., ativah c., kzE c. (kzapayati), yA c. (yApayati); ‘led a dissolute life’ vizayasuKanirato jI-vitamatyavAhayat; ‘l(ead)ing a life above their station’ svasTAnAnucitAM-svasTAnA-tiriktAM-jIvayAtrAM kalpayaMtaH.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓ(On) agre-puraH-purataH-agrataH-BU or gam 1 P or vft 1 A or sTA or car, sf 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (To) (lit.) gam, yA 2 P; ‘on the way l(ea)ing to Chitrakūta’ citrakUwayAyini vartmani (U. 1).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Cause) ex. by dat. of noun with or without BU, Avah, utpad c., jan c. (janayati); ‘advice to fools l(ead)s to their provocation’ upadeSo hi mUrKARAM prakopAya (Bavati) (H. 3).<BR>Ⓝ[Lead]ed,ⒶsIsakayukta.<BR>Ⓝ[Lead]en,Ⓒa.ⒹsIsakanirmita.<BR>Ⓝ[Lead]er,Ⓒs.ⒹnAyakaH, netf m., mArgadarSakaH, mArgopadeSakaH (lit.); muKyaH, muKaraH, agraRIH, pramuKaH, aDipaH, ISvaraH, patiH, aDyakzaH, aDipatiH, aDizWAtf m.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 purogaH-gamaH, agragaH, agra-(gre)saraH, puraHsara, purogAmin m.; ‘l(eader) of an army’ senAnIH, camUpatiH, yoDADyakzaH, senAnAyakaH; ‘l(eader) of a religious sect’ guruH, AcAryaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Lead]ership,Ⓒs.ⒹnAyakatvaM, ADipatyaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Lead]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓagraga, purogAmin, puraH-sara, purogama, prAk-agra-gAmin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 agra, agrya, muKya, utkfzwa, pramuKa, parama, uttama, praDAna in comp.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (To) Avaha, kara (rI f.) in comp.; ‘l(eading) to happiness’ kalyARAvaha, kalyARakara, kalyARodarka.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹnayaH, nIti f., netftvaM; ‘l(eading)-strings’ AlaMbanasUtrARi; ‘hold or keep in l(eading)-strings’ AtmADIna a. kf, svavaSaM nI, niyam 1 P.<BR>ⓃLed,Ⓒa.ⒹnIta, prerita, aDizWita, &c.; ‘l(ed) by’ ex. by puraHsara, purogama, pramuKa, Adi in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

