Live,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓvas 1 P, ni-prati-°; aDivas, aDyAs 2 A, aDi-zWA 1 P (with acc.).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 jIv 1 P, pra-an 2 P, Svas 2 P, Df pass. or 6 A, vid 4 A, vft 1 A; ‘here I l(ive)’ ezA Driye (U. 3); ‘as long as you l(ive)’ yAvajjIvaM, yAvatprARAn DArayasi or asuDAraRaM karozi.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (On) upa-A-jIv SarIravfttiM-prARayAtrAM-kxp c. or nirvft c. or kf 8 U, prARaDAraRaM kf, nirvah 1 P; ‘l(iv)ing on fish’ matsyAjIva, matsyopajIvin; sometimes by vftti f.; ‘l(iv)ed on fruits, roots, &c.’ PalamUlAdiBiH vfttimakarot; ‘l(iv)ing on the leaves of trees falling down of themselves’ svayaMviSIrRadrumaparRavfttitA (K. v. 28); ‘l(ive)s on wild fruits’ vanyaPalEH SarIravfttiM nirvartayati.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 jIvitaM-kAlaM gam c. (gamayati) or yA c. (yApayati) or nI 1 P or ativah c. or vft c.; ‘l(ive) through time’ cirasTAyin-amara a. BU 1 P.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹsajIva; See Living below; ‘l(ive)-long’ dIrGa-cira-kAlIna, cirasTAyin; ‘l(ive)-stock’ jIvaDanaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Liv]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹsajIva, jIvin, prARaBft, sacetana, prARaDArin, cetanAvat, sacezwa, sapramARa; ‘a l(iving) being’ prARI, jIvI, jaMtuH, prARaBft, SarIrI, jIvaH, dehI, cetanaH, sattvaM; ‘world of the l(iving)’ jIvalokaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vartamAna, DriyamARa, vidyamAna; ‘a l(iving) poet’ vartamAnakaviH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 akzaya, anaSvara, anapAyin, avinASin; ajara, amara [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=265" target="_blank">Page265</a>] (spring &c.).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 A-upa-jIvin, AjIva or vftti in comp.; ‘l(iving) by arms’ Sastropa-jIvin; ‘l(iving) by agriculture’ kfzyAjIva; ‘l(iving) wickedly’ durvftti, durvftta, pApAcarita, pApavftti; ‘l(iving) by beggary’ yAcakavftti, &c.; ‘within l(iving) memory’ smArte kAle; ‘a l(iving) sacrifice’ jIvopahAraH; ‘a l(iving) death’ jIvitamaraRaM.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹjIvanaM, prARaDAraRaM, vAsaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 jIvikA, A-upa-°; AjIvaH, vftti f., jIvanaM, vartanaM, A-upa-jIvanaM, jIvanopAyaH, jIvana-jIva-sADanaM, prARa-SarIra-yAtrA, nirvAhaH, prARa-jIva-nirvAhaH, prARa-SarIra-sTiti f., jIvanArTaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 DarmADyApakavfttiH, DarmadAyaH; ‘good