long
Long,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓ(for) (atyaMtaM) spfh 10 (with dat.), iz 6 P, aBilaz 1, 4 P, vAMC 1 P, Ih 1 A, kAMkz 1 P, ASaMs 1 A; See Wish; luB 4 P, gfD 4 P; sometimes ex. by denom. in ya or kAmya; ‘l(ong)s for a son’ putrIyati, putrakA-myati; putramIpsati, &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 dohadavatI BU 1 P, dohadinI BU.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹdIrGa, Ayata, AyAmavat, laMba, dIrGaparimARa, dIrGAkAra; vistfta, vi-stIrRa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 cira in comp., dIrGa-cira-kAlIna, dIrGa-cira-kAlika (kI f.), ciraMtana (nI f.), cirasTAyin-sTita, cirakAla-dIrGakAla-sTAyin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 dUra, vi-su-dUra.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 dIrGasUtra, cira-kriya, vilaMbakArin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 pari-pra-mARa, mAtrA, mita, parimita in comp.; ‘three fingers l(ong)’ tryaMgulamAtra-parimARa, tryaMgulamita, tryaMgula; ‘being a l(ong) way off’ dUrasTa, dUrasTAyin; ‘a l(ong) period’ dIrGa-cira-kAlaH; ‘for a l(ong) time’ ciraM, dIrGaM, cirAya; See (adv.); ‘the l(ong) run’ Ayati f.; ‘a l(ong) vowel’ dIrGasvaraH.<BR>Ⓔadv.ⒹciraM, cireRa, cirAya, dIrGa-cira-kAlaM, dIrGaM, bahukAlaM, ciradivasaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 dUraM, dUre, dUraparyaMtaM; ‘l(ong) absent’ cirapravAsin, ciragata; ‘l(ong) sick’ dIrGa-cira-rogin; ‘living l(ong)’ cirajIvin, Ayuzmat; ‘l(ong) since left’ ciratyakta, &c.; ‘how l(ong)’ kiyacciraM, kiyaMtaM kAlaM; kiyatkAlaM; ‘how l(ong) after’ kiyaccireRa; ‘not very l(ong)’ nAticiraM; ‘very l(ong)’ suciraM; ‘l(ong) ago’ prAgeva, pUrvameva, atItadIrGakAle; ‘not l(ong) ago’ nAti-cirAt prAk, anatipUrvaM; ‘ere l(ong)’ acireRa, acirAt; ‘as l(ong) as’, ‘so l(ong)’ yAvat-tAvat; ‘as l(ong) as one lives’ yAvajjIvaM; Amara-^1RAt; ‘the whole year l(ong)’ AvarzAMtAt, varzaparyaMtaM; ‘l(ong) after’ bahoH kAlAt, dIrGa-kAlAnaMtaraM. in comp. words ex. by dIrGa, cira, laMba,^2 dUra, Ayata; ‘l(ong)-armed’ dIrGaBuja, laMbahasta; ‘l(ong)-bellied’ laMbodara; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=267" target="_blank">Page267</a>] ‘l(ong)-continuing’ cirasTAyin; ‘l(ong)-eyed’ AyatAkza, Ayatanetra; ‘l(ong)-headed’ sUkzma nipuRa-mati, vidagDa, pawu; ‘l(ong)-lasting’ cirasTAyin, cirakAlika; See (a.); ‘l(ong)-legged’ dIrGapAda, UrDvajAnu, UrDvajYu; ‘l(ong)-lived’ cira(ra)jIvin, dIrGAyus, cirAyus, cirAyuzya, jEvAtfka, Ayuzmat; ‘l(ong) pepper’ kfzRA, upakulyA, vEdehI, mAgaDI, capalA, kaRA, u(U)zaRA, pippaliH-lI, SOMqI, kolA; karipippalI, kapivallI, kolavallI, SreyasI, vaSiraH; ‘l(ong) pepper root’ graMTikaM, pippalImUlaM, cawakASiras n.; ‘l(ong)-sighted’ dUra-dIrGa-dfzwi; ‘l(ong)-suffering’ sahizRu, sahanaSIla, kzamin, bahukzama; (s.) kzamA, sahizRutA, sahanaSIlatA.<BR>Ⓝ[Long]er,Ⓒa.ⒹdIrGatara; ‘any l(onger)’ ataHparaM-UrDvaM, itaH paraM; ‘why delay any l(onerg)’ kimityaDunA vilaMbyate.<BR>Ⓝ[Long]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹatyaBilAzin, atyAkAMkzin; kutUhalin, spfhayAlu, utkaMWita, utkawa, lAlasa, atyutsuka; ‘a l(onging) desire’ utkawecCA; ‘a l(onging) woman’ SradDAluH; dohadavatI.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹatyaBilAzaH, atispfhA-vAMCA, atyAkAMkzA, utkaMWA, lAlasA, OtsukyaM, atilipsA; icCA^3; kAmaH, manoraTaH, spfhA, tfzRA, A-kAMkzA; ‘the l(onging) of a pregnant woman’ dohadaH, garBadohadaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Long]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsaspfhaM, satfzRaM, sotsukaM, sotkaMWaM.<BR>ⓃLonganimity,Ⓒs.ⒹkzamA, kzAMti f.<BR>ⓃLongeval, Longevous,Ⓒa.ⒹciraMjIvin; See Long-lived.<BR>ⓃLongevity,Ⓒs.ⒹdIrGAyuH; cirAyuH.<BR>ⓃLongmetry,Ⓒs.ⒹdErGyamAnaM.<BR>ⓃLength,Ⓒs.ⒹdErGyaM, dIrGatA-tvaM, AyAmaH, drAGiman m., ArohaH, Ayati f., vistAraH, AnAhaH, vistfti f., vitati f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mAtrA, avaDiH, maryAdA, paryaMtaH; ‘my rudeness (impudence) was carried to the l(ength) of taking up arms’ AyuDa parigrahaM yAvadatyArUQo duryogaH (U. 6).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 mAnaM, pra-pari-mARaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 cira-dIrGa-kAlaH, kAla-dErGyaM; ‘to such a l(ength)’ etAvatparyaMtaM, yAvat (with acc.); ‘for a l(ength) of time’ ciraM, cirakAlaM; ‘to a great l(ength)’ atimAtraM, ati-maryAdaM; ‘at l(ength)’ savistaraM, vistareRa, suvistaraM -reRa, vistaraSaH^4, asaMkzepataH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aMte, aMtataH, Seze, cirakAlAt, cirasya, atItadIrGakAle. ‘spread at l(ength)’ vistIrRa; ‘to lie at full l(ength)’ daMqavat pat 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Length]en,Ⓒv. t.ⒹdIrGIkf 8 U, pra-vi-tan 8 U, vistF c., pra-vi-sf c., Ayam 1 A, AyatI-vitatI-kf.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹvistF-vitan- pass., dIrGIBU.<BR>Ⓝ[Length]wise,Ⓒadv.ⒹanvAyAmaM, anudErGyaM, anu in comp.<BR>Ⓝ[Length]y,Ⓒa.ⒹvistIrRa, dIrGa, Ayata, savistara, asaMkzipta.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170120. note: missing '-'. full word AmaraRAt.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20161215.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by  on 20161215.<BR>[4] Correction submitted by  on 20170120. note: indicates 3s ending of prev. line 'suvistaraM'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

