look
Look (at),Ⓒv. i.ⒹdfS 1 P, ava-vi-A-lok 1 A, 10, Ikz 1 A, nirUp 10, nirvarR 10, dfzwiM dA 3 U or kzip 6 P, lakz 10; ‘l(ook) intently at’ nayanEH-dfzwiBiH-pA 1 P, niDyE 1 P, (tA rAGavaM dfzwiBirApibaMtyaH &c. R. vii. 12).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 BA 2 P, A-prati-°, lakz-dfS- pass.; oft. by vadana, muKa, Anana in comp.; ‘she l(ook)s sad’ vizaRRA lakzyate or ABAti, &c.; ‘that l(ook)s like wantonness’ tatsAhasABAsaM (Mal. 2); ‘l(ook)ing dejected’ vizaRRavadana, mlAnamuKa, &c.; ‘l(ook) well’ SuB 1 A; ‘l(ook) now’ nanu, paSya.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] about,Ⓐparito vIkz, anu-iz 4 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] after,Ⓐavekz, rakz 1 P, pA c. (pAlayati); See ‘Take care’ under Care; yogakzemaM vah 1 U, (mugDAyA me jananyA yogakzemaM vahasva M. 4).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anviz; nirUp 10, mfg 10 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] down,Ⓐavekz, aDo dfS; ‘l(ook) down upon’ avaman 4 A, upekz; See Contemn.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] for,ⒶASaMs 1 A, apekz, prati-iz 6 P. See Expect.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2. anviz, mfg; See Search.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] in,ⒶAvirBU 1 P, AtmAnaM dfS c., prakawIBU; ‘l(ook) in the face’ saMmuKI-aBimuKI-BU (with gen.); See Face.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] into,Ⓐava-saM-nir-pari-Ikz, anusaM-DA 3 U, nirUp; See Examine; ‘l(ook) into the matter very closely’ atinipuRamavekzyatAM sorTaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] on,Ⓐprekz, miz 6 P; mizatAmAcCinatti naH (K. ii. 46) ‘snatches (the oblation), we helplessly l(ook)ing on’<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Upon) man 4 A, gaR 10; See Consider.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] out,ⒶavaDA 3 U, sAvaDAna a. BU 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] over,ⒶsaMdfS-Ikz; nirUp, nirIkz.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] to,ⒶsaM-vi-Ikz, avaDAnaM dA 3 U; ex. by ‘Care’ q. v.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 A-ava-laMb 1 A, ASri 1 U.<BR>Ⓝ[Look] up,ⒶUrDvaM, dfS or Ikz, udIkz, unmuKIBU; ‘l(ook)ing up to heaven’ naBodatta-dfzwi, gaganadfzwi; ‘l(ook) up to’ pratIkz, ud-dfS; man, gaR, parikxp c., ‘the people l(ook) up to you as their saviour’ Atmanorakzakatvena tvAmevAmI janAH pratIkzaMte, gaRayaMti or pari-kalpayaMti.<BR>Ⓔs.Ⓓdfzwi f., darSanaM, IkzaRaM, vIkzaRaM, prekzaRaM, vIkzitaM, vilokitaM, A-vi-ava-lokanaM, dfzwipAtaH, dfkpAtaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 rUpaM, AkAraH, Akfti f., darSanaM, AlokaH, caryA, ABA, CAyA, vadanAkAraH, muKacCAyA, muKaM, vadanaM; ‘a l(ook) of displeasure’ akfpAdfzwiH; ‘side-l(ook)’ kawAkzaH; apAMgadarSanaM; ‘l(ook)-out’ avekzA, samIkzA, avaDAnaM; ‘to be on the l(ook) out’ avekz, avaDA 3 U, avahita a. BU.<BR>Ⓝ[Look]er,Ⓒs.Ⓓdrazwf m., darSin m., vIkzakaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (On) prekzakaH, prekzamARaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Look]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹpaSyat, darSin; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=268" target="_blank">Page268</a>] dfzwi, nayana in comp.; ‘l(ook) in all directions’, vizvagdfzwi; sarvato dattadfzwi; ‘l(ook) up’ unmuKa, UrDvadfzwi ‘l(ook) well’ SuBa-su-darSana, sudfSya, SoBanAkAra, prekzaRIya, SuBAnana.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹdarSanaM, vilokanaM, vIkzaRaM, nirvarRanaM, AlokaH, &c. See (s.) above; ‘l(ooking)-glass’ AdarSaH, mukuraH, darpaRaH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

