lose
Lose,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓapa-, hf c., tyaj 1 P, hA 3 P or c. (hApayati).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 viyuj-vihA-parihA- pass., vinAkf 8 U, (with instr.); BraMS 1 A, 4 P, pari-pra°, cyu 1 A, pra-vi-°, (with abl.); See Deprived also; ‘he lost his life’ prARErviyuktaH, vigatAsurbaBUva, prARahInaH, prARErahIyata; ‘lost his realm’ rAjyAdBrazwaH-cyutaH; ‘l(ose)s his friends’ mi-trErviyujyate; ‘he lost his wife’ tatpatnI mftA, patnyA virahitaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Destroy) naS c., kzi 1, 5 P or c., apa-ci 5 U, ucCid 7 P, pra-vi-DvaMs c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 (Not to find) ex. by naS 4 P, praBraMS; ‘have you lost a camel’ api yuzmAkamuzwro nazwaH; ‘the lost ring’ nazwamaMgulIyakaM; ‘l(ose) the way’ mArgAt or paTaH-BraMS or cyu or vical 1 P; ‘he lost his way’ praBrazwa nazwa-paTaH or unmArga-gAmI aBUt; ‘lost his caste’ jAterBrazwaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 parAji-parABU- pass. (in battle &c.); ‘l(ose) oneʼs wits’ budDihIna a. BU ‘to l(ose) time’ kAlaM vyarTaM nI 1 P or vikzip 6 P, kAlaM hf 1 P or yA c. (yApayati), kAlaharaRaM-kAla-kzepaM kf 8 U, vilaMb 1 A; ‘l(ose) good name’ cAritryaM-kIrtiM kalaMkayati or malinayati (D.) or duz c. (dUzayati); ‘l(ose) oneʼs consciousness’ muh 4 P, murC 1 P, cetanAM-saMjYAM hA, nazwacetana-luptasaMjYa a. BU; ‘we donʼt l(ose) anything (in this way)’ na naH kiMcit Cidyate (S. B. 345), nAsmAkaM ki-mapi hIyate; ‘to l(ose) oneself in’ Asakta-nirata a. BU; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=269" target="_blank">Page269</a>] See Absorb.<BR>Ⓝ[Los]er,Ⓒs.ⒹprAptA-pAyaH, apAya-hAni-sahaH, parAjitaH, labDa-hAniH; prAptanASaH-kzayaH.<BR>ⓃLost,Ⓒa.Ⓓnazwa, Brazwa, cyuta, gata, vIta, hIna, tyakta, hfta, hArita, kzIRa, lupta; ‘who has l(ost) his office’ cyutADikAraH, aDikAraBrazwaH, ‘who has l(ost) wealth’ arTahInaH, gataviBavaH, nazwArTaH; ‘who has l(ost) his way’ paTaBrazwaH, unmArga-pravfttaH, diNmUQaH; ‘who has l(ost) everything’ hftasarvasvaH; ‘who has l(ost) one eye’ akzRA aMDaH, ekAkzivikalaH; ‘l(ost) to shame’ tyakta-nirasta-lajja, vrIqAhIna, ‘l(ost) to sense of freedom’ svAtaMtryarasAnaBijYa; ‘l(ost) in meditation’ DyAnapara-parA-yaRa-nizWa-magna ciMtAsakta; ‘the bone fell and was l(ost)’ asTi nipatitaM nayanavizayA-tItaM ca; ‘to be l(ost)’ naS, aMtar-i, tiroDA pass., tiroBU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mohita, mUQa, BrAMta-citta-budDi.<BR>ⓃLoss,Ⓒs.ⒹhAni f., kzayaH, saM-upa-pari-kzayaH, vi-, nASaH, apAyaH, apacayaH, lopaH, BraMSaH, cyuti f., vyayaH, DvaMsaH, pra-vi-DvaMsaH, viyogaH, apahAraH, atyayaH, tyAgaH, alABaH, kzati f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 parAjayaH, parABavaH, BaMgaH; ‘compensating l(oss)’ kzatipUraRaM; ‘profit and l(oss)’ lABAlABO; ‘l(oss) of time’ kAla-haraRaM-kzepaH, vilaMbaH; ‘l(oss) of caste’ jAti-BraMSaH; ‘l(oss) of army’ sEnyanASaH, balavyasanaM; ‘to be at a l(oss)’ muh 4 P; ‘being at a l(oss) what to do or say’ kiMkartavyatA-kiMvaktavyatA-mUQa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

