aRayin m., anurAgin m., nirataH, sevI-priyaH in comp.; ‘l(over) of knowledge’ priyajYAnaH, jYAnanirataH, jYAnepsuH; ‘a l(over) of learned men’ AgamavfdDasevI (R. vi. 41).<BR>Ⓝ[Lov]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹpraRayin, anurAgavat, sasneha, praRayavat, prItimat, vatsala, anurakta, anurAgin, Asakta, priya, ni-, rata, sevin in comp.; ‘l(oving) gambling’ dyUtAsakta, dyUtasevin; ‘a l(oving) husband’ anurAgavAn patiH; ‘l(oving) kindness’ kfpA, dayA, kAruRyaM, vAtsalyaM, prasAdaH, anugrahaH, snehaH, anukaMpA.<BR>Ⓝ[Lov]ingly,Ⓒadv.Ⓓsa-praRayaM, sasnehaM, sAnurAgaM, snehena, vAtsalyAt, prItipUrvaM.<BR>ⓃLovely,Ⓒa.ⒹkAMta, suMdara (rI f.), rucira, SoBana, suBaga, manojYa, maMju, maMjula, cAru, manorama, manohara, lalita, vAma, mugDa, kamanIya, aBirAma; See Beautiful.<BR>Ⓝ[Love]liness,Ⓒs.ⒹkAMti f., sOMdaryaM, SoBA, SrIH, lAvaRyaM, suBagatA, cArutA; See Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

