mean
Mean,Ⓒa.ⒹmaDya, maDyaparimARa-pramARa, maDyama.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 maDya, maDyama, maDyasTita, vyavahita, maDyavartin, aMtargata; ‘in the m(ean)-while’ ‘in the m(ean)-time’ atrAMtare.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 nIca, apa-ni-kfzwa, aDama, jaGanya, kadarya, kutsita, ni-, hIna, anArya, Kala, duzwa, vivarRa, pAmara, prAkfta, apasada, kzullaka, yApya, avama, avadya, garhya, laGu, kupUya, Kewa in comp., aRaka, rePa; tucCa, kzudra, kfpaRa, dIna, (mind &c.); (in birth) hIna-nIca-jAti, aMtyajAtIya, akulIna, ku or kA in comp.; ‘m(ean)-spirited’ laGucetas, kzudramAnasa, kfpaRabudDi, kApuruza, aDamavftti.<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹuddiS 6 P, iz 6 P, aBipra-i 2 P; oft. ex. by desid. forms, or by kAma or manas in comp. with inf.; ‘now what do you m(ean) to do’ aTa BavAn kiM kartumanAH or kiM cikIrzati; See Intend.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 gam c. (gamayati), buD c., dyut c., aBi-DA 3 U, sUc 10, nirdiS; gen. ex. by vft 1 A with loc., or by loc. simply; by arTa, para, vAcin in comp.; jyotiH-Sabdastejasi vartate (S. B. 146); atra apacitiSabdaH pUjArTaH-pUjAparaH-pUjAvAcI &c.; ‘a speech m(ean)ing censure’ niMdAparaM vacaH; ‘what is meant by telling a lie’ asatyamitti yaducyate tena kiM gamyate, or asatyaBAzaRasya korTaH; ‘what can all this m(ean)’ kaH prakAraH, kimetat (Mal. 5), kiM nu etatsyAt (Mal. 1).<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹmaDyamaparimARaM, maDyatA, maDyaM, samapramARaM, sama-pakzaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aMtaraM, aByaMtaraM, maDyAvaDiH, aMtarAlaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 parimitatA, anatikramaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 (Means) sA-DanaM, upakaraRaM, upAyaH, karaRaM, dvAraM, yogaH, gati f., sAhAyyaM, sAmagrI, kAraRaM, hetuH; oft. ex. by instr.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 AyaH, viBavaH; dravyaM, DanaM, sAmarTyaM, Sakti f., DanAgamaH; ‘donʼt live beyond your m(eans)’ AyamaryAdAM mAtikrAma, yaTAviBavaM-yaTASakti &c. vyayaM kuru; ‘having moderate m(eans)’ nAtiDana, alpaviBava; ‘by all m(eans)’ sarvaTA, sarvaprakAreRa, avaSyaM, nUnaM, Kalu, avaSyameva; ‘by no m(eans)’ na sarvaTA, na kaTaMcana, na kaTaMcit; ‘by any m(eans)’ yena kena prakAreRa, yaTA kaTaMcit, kaTamapi, kaTaM-cana, kaTaMcit, kaTaM kaTamapi; ‘m(eans) of subsistence’ jIvana-sADanaM-upAyaH-hetuH; upajIvikA.<BR>Ⓝ[Mean]ing,Ⓒs.ⒹaBiprAyaH, uddeSaH, ASayaH, arTaH, tAtparyaM, BAvaH, AkUtaM, iMgitaM, AkAMkzA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vivakzA, vivakzitaM, arTaH; ‘the m(eaning) of a word’ padArTaH; ‘literal m(eaning)’ a-vayavArTaH, padArTaH, SabdArTaH; ‘hidden m(eaning)’ marman n., gUQArTaH; ‘what is the m(eaning) of this laughter’ kiMnimittoyaM hAsaH.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹarTavat, sArTa, pUrRArTa, caritArTa, sAkUta; ‘casting at me a m(eaning) look’ sAkUtaM mAM nirvarRya.<BR>Ⓝ[Mean]ingless,Ⓒa.ⒹnirarTaka, anarTaka, nizkAraRa, animitta.<BR>Ⓝ[Mean]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsArTaM, sAkUtaM, seMgitaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Mean]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹkfpaRavat, aDamavat, dInaM, &c.; sAvajYaM, sAvamAnaM, lAGavena; ‘m(eanly) born’ hInajAti, aDamavarRa; ‘m(eanly) attired’ kfpaRa-anArya-veza.<BR>Ⓝ[Mean]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹnIcatA, aDamatA, kadaryatA, kutsitatA, &c.; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=283" target="_blank">Page283</a>] ‘m(eanness) of birth’ akulInatA, apakfzwaM janma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

