levity n(atural) to mortals’ mAnuzatAsulaBo laGimA (Ka. 134).<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹmUQaH, mUrKaH, jaqaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Natural]ist,Ⓒs.ⒹpadArTa-SAstrajYaH, padArTavijYAnin m.<BR>Ⓝ[Natural]ize,Ⓒv. t.ⒹaByas 4 U; See Familiarize.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 deSIya a. kf 8 U.<BR>Ⓝ[Natural]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹprakftyA, nisargeRa, svaBAvataH, svaBAvena, nisargataH, jAtyA, (s.) in comp.; ‘n(aturally) charming’ nisargamaDura, prakftisuBaga, avyAjasuMdara-manohara, &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 yaTAkramaM, anu-lomaM, sfzwikramAnusAreRa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 akftrimaM, aklizwaM, ayatnataH, sahajaSaktyA-gatyA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 svataH, svayaM, aMtaHpravfttyA, abalAt, sahajAvaboDena.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 avaSyaM, nirvivAdaM, niyataM, anAyAsenEva; nUnaM, Kalu.<BR>Ⓝ[Natural]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹsahajatvaM, akftakatA, yATArTyaM, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

