object
Object,Ⓒs.ⒹdravyaM, vastu n., arTaH, vizayaH, iMdri-yArTaH; ‘visible o(bject)’ cakzurvizayaH; (fig.) pAtraM, padaM, sTAnaM, AspadaM, BAjanaM, BUmi f., vizayaH; ‘o(bject) of contidence’ viSvAsAspadaM, viSvAsaBUmiH; ‘the sole o(bject) of my affection’ snehasyEkAyanIBUtA (M. 2); ‘o(bject) of dispute’ vivAdavizayaH, vyavahArAspadaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 arTaH, PalaM, hetuH; (‘desired o(bject)’) aBIzwaM, izwaM, samIhitaM, kAMkzitaM, IpsitaM, kAmaH, mano-raTaH; See Desire.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 nimittaM, kAraRaM, prayo-janaM, kAryaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 aBiprAyaH, ASayaH, tAtparyaM, uddeSaH, lakzyaM; ‘with what o(bject) in view’ kimapekzya PalaM, kena hetunA, kimuddiSya, kiM-nimittaM, kimarTaM; ‘accomplishment of oneʼs o(bject)’ kftArTatA, caritArTatA, izwasidDi f., PalaprApti f.; ‘highest o(bject)’ paramArTaH; ‘o(bject) of hearing’ SrutivizayaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 karman n.; ‘a root governing two o(bject)s’ dvikarmakaH DAtuH.<BR>Ⓔv.Ⓓvi-prati-ruD 7 U, bAD 1 A, KaMq 10, niras 4 U, aDarIkf 8 U, apavad 1 A, na anumana 4 A or anumud 1 A, dozaM grah 9 U, ‘the sage will not o(bject) to this’ nAtra dozaM grahIzyati kulapatiH (S. 3); ni-prati-ziD 1 P, (tadeza sargaH na BavadBiH pratizeDanIyaH R. xiv. 42); in discussions gen. ex. by nanu, iti cet or kaTaM tarhi, followed by ucyate or atrocyate (we reply); pratyavasTA 1 A, vitaMq 1 A.<BR>Ⓝ[Object]ion,Ⓒs.ⒹbADaH-DA, apavAdaH, viroDaH, A-kzepaH, dozaH, Apatti f., kakzA, udgrAhaH, virudDahetuH, vipratizeDaH, pratyavAyaH, pratibaMDaH, paryudAsaH, ‘making an o(bjection)’ dozagrahaRaM, viroDopanyAsaH; ‘settling an o(bjection)’ samA-pratisamA-DAnaM, AkzepaparihAraH.<BR>Ⓝ[Object]ionable,Ⓒa.ⒹbADya, sabADa, sadoza, nizeDArha, varjya, parihArya, ASaMkanIya.<BR>Ⓝ[Object]ive,Ⓒa.ⒹvizayASrita, padArTanizWa, karmavizayaka.<BR>Ⓝ[Object]or,Ⓒs.ⒹbADakaH, apavAdakaH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

