oblige
Oblige,Ⓒv. t.ⒹEx. by causal of verbs, gen. with balena or balAt; prayuj 10, pravft c.; See Compel.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 niyamapUrvaM-sapra-tijYaM baMD 9 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 anugrah 9 P, upakf 8 U, upakAreRa baMD, hitaM-prasAdaM-upakAraM kf; ‘I am much o(blig)ed to you for this reward’ etena pAritozikadAnena BavatA sutarAmupakf-tosmi-anugfhItosmi; ‘I am much o(blig)ed’ anugfhItosmi, mahAnayaM prasAdaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Oblig]ation,Ⓒs.ⒹavaSyakatA, kartavyatA, BAraH, fRaM, baMDaH, DarmaH; ‘free from the o(bligation)s of debt’ fRamukta, muktarRa, anfRa; ‘religious o(bligation)’ vrataM, niyamaH, codanA, viDiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMvid f., samayaH, pratijYA, niyamaH, aByupagamaH, saMDA, saM-A-SravaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 anugrahaH, upakAraH, upakfti f. -taM, hitaM, priyaM; ‘under o(bligation)’ upakfta-anugfhIta a.; ‘my o(bligation)s to you are immense’ tava mayi upakArAH saM-KyAtItAH; ‘to lay under o(bligation)s’ upakf; See (v.).<BR>Ⓝ[Oblig]atory,Ⓒa.ⒹavaSyaka AvaSyaka (kI f.), aparihArya, avaSyakartavya; oft. ex. by avaSyaM; See under Compel.<BR>Ⓝ[Oblig]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓanugraha-upakAra-SIla, upakArin, anugrAhin, hita-upakAra-budDi, suSIla, dakziRa, anukUla, sujana.<BR>Ⓝ[Oblig]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹdAkziRyena, sujana-tayA, sAnugrahaM, suSIlavat.<BR>Ⓝ[Oblig]ingness,Ⓒs.ⒹupakAra-anugraha-SIlaM, sOjanyaM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

