pass
Pass,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓati-vyati-i 2 P, atikram 1 U, 4 P; ‘they two p(ass)ed each other’ parasparamatItya-ullaMGyatO nirgatO; tF 1 P, saM-ut-niH-°, ut-, laMG 1 A, 10, pAraM gam 1 P, atigam; ‘p(ass)ed his examination’ parIkzApAraM gataH, parIkzAmuttatAra.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Time) gam c. (gamayati), nI 1 P, ati-vah c., kzE c. (kzapayati), yA c. (yApayati); ‘he with difficulty p(ass)ed eight years’ tenAzwO pari-gamitAH samAH kaTaMcit (R. viii. 92); ‘p(ass)ing (staying for) three nights’ tisro vasatIruzitvA (R. vii. 33).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 saM-, car-l c., saMkram c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 nizpad c., vyavasTA c. (sTApayati), siD c. (sADayati); saM-anu-man 4 A, parigrah 9 P (bill &c.); ‘p(ass) sentence’ nirRayaM dA 3 U, daMqaM AdiS 6 P; ‘this p(ass)es conception’ vicAra-vizayAtikrAMtametat, DiyaH paTi na vartate.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓgam, i-yA- 2 P, cal-car 1 P, pra-, sf 1 P, ati-vyati-i, atikram; ‘let it p(ass) now’ tizWatu tadaDunA, yAtu, kimanena.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pra-cal-i, pracalita a. BU 1 P, pra-sf, pracalIBU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 siD 4 P, nizpannI-sidDIBU, anu-saM-man pass.; parigrah pass.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 upa-, saMkram, saMcar.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 saMvft 1 A, samA-pad 4 A, saM-, BU, A-pat 1 P, Gaw 1 A; See Happen, Occur.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] away,Ⓐati-vyati-i, gam, yA, atikram, ativft.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pra-, naS 4 P, pra-vi-lI 4 A, tiroBU, kzi pass., kzar 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] by,Ⓐatikram, ati-i, aticar, ullaMG.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 upekz 1 A, na gaR 10, tyaj 1 P, apAs 4 U; See Neglect.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] for,ⒶEx. by denominatives; eraMqopi drumAyate ‘p(ass)es for a tree’; man-gaR- pass.; ‘he p(asse)s for a learned man’ paMqita iti manyate (janEH).<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] into,ⒶniviS-praviS- 6 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] off,Ⓐapa-i, apa-yA-gam, vigam.<BR>Ⓔ(v. t.)Ⓓvi-BU c., saMdfS c., Akal 10; ‘tried to p(ass) the matter off with a joke’ taM vfttAMtaM parihAsamiva gaRayituM-AkalayituM-yete; hfdaya-vallaBo'BiliKya kAmadevavyapadeSena saKIpurato'pahnataH (Rat. 2) ‘p(ass)ed off the picture of her beloved upon her friend as that of Cupid’.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] on,Ⓐpra-vft, pra-yA-gam-sf.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] over,Ⓐupekz, utsfj 6 P, tyaj, na gaR laMG, ati-i-atikram, atikramya gam, tF; See (v. t.); aMtarayati (D.), maDyamAMbAvfttAMtoM'tarita AryeRa (U. 1) ‘is p(ass)ed over’ &c.; oft. by sTA, As 2 A with tAvat; ‘let us p(ass) over this sad tale’ tizWatu-AstAM-tAvadayaM [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=333" target="_blank">Page333</a>] duHKavfttAMtaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass] through,ⒶnirBid 7 P, praviSya nirgam; (throughts &c.) See Occur.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹsaMkawaM, saMkramaH, saMcaraH, saMkawa or saMbADa-paTaH or mArgaH, durgasaMcaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 darI, vidaraH, raMDraM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Passport) anujYA, anumati f., anujYApatraM, mudrA; ‘why do you leave the camp without (taking) a p(ass)’ kimarTamagfhItamudraH kawakA-nnizkrAmasi; ‘without a p(ass)’ amudrAlAMCitaH (Mu. 2).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 prahAraH, AGAtaH, tAqanaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 daSA, avasTA, sTiti f., durdaSA, durgati f., kazwaM, kfcCraM, kazwAvasTA.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass]able,Ⓒa.Ⓓgamya, tArya, sugama, ullaMGya; ‘not p(assable)’ durgama, agamya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sahya, soQavya, upekzaRIya, viguRa.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass]age,Ⓒs.ⒹgamanaM, taraRaM, yAnaM; ‘p(assage) through the world’ lokayAtrA, saMsArapaTaH, ‘p(assage) to and fro’ gamanAgamanaM, yAtAyAtaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 mArgaH; See Way.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 saMkramaH, saMcAraH, atikramaH, pAragamanaM, ullaM-GanaM; See (s.).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 gamana-saMkramaRa-kAlaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 saMcaraH, saMkramaH, durgasaMcaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 gamanADikAraH, anujYA-patraM-mudrA; See Pass.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 vacanaM, sTAnaM, sTalaM, deSaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 vfttaM, BUtaM, vfttAMtaH; ‘p(assage)-money’ AtA(ta)raH, taramUlyaM-paRyaM, tArikaM, tAryaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass]ed,Ⓒa.ⒹatIta, gata, saMkrAMta, vIta, tIrRa, sidDa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (As excrement) uccArita, hanna, gUna.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass]er,Ⓒs.,Ⓓ(‘p(asser)-by’), paTikaH, aDvagaH, pAMTaH; See Traveller.<BR>Ⓝ[Pass]ing,Ⓒs.ⒹtaraRaM, gamanaM, calanaM.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹgAmin, yAyin in comp.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 atikrAmaka.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 uttama, parama, SrezWa, viSizwa.<BR>Ⓔadv.ⒹatIva, atimAtraM, nitAMtaM, ati pr., atiSaya in comp.<BR>ⓃPassenger,Ⓒs.ⒹtaraH, taritf m., uttaraRakft.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 nO or pota-gAmI or yAyI.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 paTikaH, yAtrikaH, pAMTaH; See Traveller.<BR>ⓃPast,Ⓒa.Ⓓgata, atIta, BUta, vyatIta, atikrAMta, vftta, parokza; ‘p(ast) time’ BUtakAlaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pUrva, pUrvatana (nI f.); ‘in p(ast) times’ purA, pUrvaM, purAkalpe.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 sidDa, nizpanna, samApta, kfta.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹBUtaM, atItaM, samatItaM, atikrAMtaM, gata-atIta-BUta-kAlaH.<BR>Ⓔprep.,Ⓓati pr., atIta, atikrAMta, nazwa, hIna in comp., a-nir pr.; ‘p(ast) cure’ asADya, nirupacAra; ‘p(ast) the range of sight’ cakzurvizayAtikrAMta, nayanapaTAtIta; ‘p(ast) all shame’ nirlajja, nazwa-tyakta-lajja; ‘p(ast) human strength’ atimAnuzaSakti; See Beyond also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passible
