please
Please,Ⓒv. t.ⒹprI 9 P, 10 (prIRayati), tfp c., saM-pari-°, ram c. (ramayati), pramud c., suKayati (D.), A-naMd c., saM-, tuz c., prasad c., AhlAd c., hfz c., ArAD c., anuraMj c.; oft. by icCA, prasAdaH, kfpA; vizamapyamftaM kvacidBavedamftaM vA vizamISvarecCayA (R. viii. 46) ‘if it p(lease) God to do so’ &c.; ‘he was p(leas)ed to accept my presents’ mamopAyanAni sa suprItamanasA-suprasannaM-svIcakAra; ‘may it p(lease) your ladyship’ prasIdatu BawwinI (M. 4).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Like) See below.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓ‘to be p(leas)ed’ tuz 4 P, tfp 4 P; ram-mud 1 A, naMd 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 arh 1 P or prasad 1 P, with inf., or simply by Imperative; ‘p(lease) sit here’ atropavi-SatvAryaH; ‘worthy Sir, p(lease) to wait for 2 or 3 days’ dvitrARyahAnyarhasi soQumarhan (R. v. 25).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 ruc 1 A, iz 6 P; See Like; ‘just as my friend p(lease)s’ yadaBi-rocate vayasyAya; ‘do as you p(lease)’ yaTABilazitaM kriyatAM.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]ance,Ⓒs.ⒹkrIqodyAna.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]ant,Ⓒa.ⒹsuKakara (rI f.), maDura, suKada-prada, suKAvaha, ramya, ramaRIya, priya, manohara-rama, aBirAma, suBaga, aBimata, suKa, kAmya, kAMta, harzAvaha, rucira, hfdya, hfdayaMgama, prIti-tuzwi-kara, manojYa, maMjula, cAru; ‘a p(leasant) joke’ hfdayaMgamaH parihAsaH (Mal. 3).<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]antly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsuKaM, ramyaM, maDuraM, priyaM, ruciraM.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]antry,Ⓒs.Ⓓpari(rI)hAsaH, narmaBAzitaM, vinodaH, narmAlApaH, vinoda-narma-ukti f.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹsuKa in comp.; ramya, kAMta; See Pleasant, ‘p(leasing) to the ear’ suKaSrava, SrutisuKa, maMjula-svana, suSrAvya; ‘p(leasing) to the eye’ prekzaRIya, nayanABirAma, sudfSya; ‘p(leasing) language’ cAwu m. n., cAwUktiH.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleas]ingly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsuBagaM, suKaM, suKa-cAru in comp.<BR>ⓃPleasure,Ⓒs.ⒹsuKaM, saM-pari-tozaH, AnaMdaH, prIti f., sOKyaM, tuzwi f., pra-, modaH, AhlAdaH, harzaH, mudA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aBi-, ruci f., icCA, aBilAzaH, CaMdaH-das n., kAmaH; ‘at oneʼs p(leasure)’ svecCayA, kAmataH, yaTAkAmaM, yadfcCayA, svEraM; ‘wandering at p(leasure)’ kAmacArin^1, svacCaMda-gAmin; ‘sensual p(leasure)’ BogaH, vizayasuKaM, vizayAnurAgaH; ‘sexual p(leasure)’ rati f., rati-suKaM, su-, rataM; ‘p(leasure)-boat’ keli-krIqA-nOkA; ‘p(leasure)-ground’ ArAmaH, krIqA-keli-vilAsa-vanaM-kAnanaM, pramadavanaM, krIqodyAnaM; ‘p(leasure)-mansion’ keligfhaM-BavanaM, lIlAgAraM, vilAsamaMdiraM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 prasAdaH, anugrahaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleasur]able,Ⓒa.Ⓓramya, ramaRIya, suKada, suKa; See Pleasant.<BR>Ⓝ[Pleasur]ist,Ⓒs.Ⓓvizayin m., vizayAsaktaH, BogA-saktaH, BogaparAyaRaH.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

