, deya, darSanIya, praveSya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pAMkteya, pAMktya, saBya.<BR>Ⓝ[Present]ation,Ⓒs.ⒹupaharaRaM, arpaRaM, pratipAdanaM, dAnaM; ‘p(resentation) of an oblation’ bali-dAnaM, nirvapaRaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Present]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹaDunA, saMprati, sAMprataM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sapadi, anaMtaraM, drAk, tatkzaRaM-Re, tatkAle, sadyaH, acirAt, SIGraM, ASu, Jawiti.<BR>ⓃPresence,Ⓒs.ⒹsanniDiH^1, samupasTiti f., upasTAnaM, sAMniDyaM, sanniDAnaM, pratyakzatA, samakzatA, ABimuKyaM; ‘in the p(resence) of’ samakzaM, pratyakzaM, saMmuKaM, sAkzAt, in comp. or with gen.; ‘in the p(resence) of fire’ agniM sAkzye ADAya (R. vii. 20); ‘into the p(resence) of’ sakASaM-Se, samIpaM-pe, aMtikaM, in comp. or with gen.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 AkAraH, Akfti f., rUpaM, SarIrasaMsTA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Of mind) pratyutpannamati f., pratiBA, pratiBAnaM, pratiBAnavattvaM, samAhitatvaM, avyagratA, asaMBramaH, nirAkulatvaM; ‘p(resence)-chamber’ darSana-SAlA, AsTAnaM-nI.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

