relate
Relate,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓ(To) uddiS 6 P, apekz 1 A, anuzaMj-saMbaMD pass.; by deriv. in Iya, or vizaya in comp.; ‘r(elat)ing to Sastras’ SAstrIya, SAstravizaya; ‘news r(elat)ing to the kingʼs murder’ rAjaGAta vizayakaH-saMbadDaH-vfttAMtaH; See Refer.<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹkaT 10, AKyA 2 P, varR 10, SaMs 1 P, cakz 2 A, A-ni-vid c.; See Tell.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ed,Ⓒa.ⒹkaTita, KyAta, varRita, &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saM-anu-badDa, anuzakta, anvita, saMsakta, saMpfkta, saMbaMDin, saMparkin, in comp.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 saMbaMDin, sajAti, sajAtIya, eka-sa-gotra, sakulya, gotraja, ekaSarIrAnvaya.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]er,Ⓒs.ⒹAKyAyakaH, kaTayitf m.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓ(To) saMbaMDin, vizaya in comp.; See Refer.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ion,Ⓒs.ⒹsaMbaMDaH, anvayaH, saMdarBaH, saMsargaH, saMparkaH, anuzaMgaH, BAvaH; ‘mutual r(elation)’ vyatizaMgaH, anyonyasaMbaMDaH, AkAMkzA (between a word and its meaning); ‘intimate r(elation)’ samavAya-nitya-saMbaMDaH; ‘the r(elaion) of the container and the thing contained’ ADArADeyaBAvaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 baMDutA, jYAtiBAvaH, SarIrasaMbaMDaH, SarIrAnvayaH, sajAtitvaM, sagotratA, sapiMqatA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 baMDuH, bAMDavaH, jYAtiH, gotrajaH, sagotrajaH, sakulyaH, saMbaMDI, sapiMqaH (to the 7th degrees), samAnodakaH (8th to 14th degree); sanABiH, sodaryaH, samAnodaraH (by blood); ‘r(elation)s collectively’ bAMDavagaRaH-janaH, baMDu-jYAti-vargaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 A-upA-KyAnaM, varRanaM, kaTanaM, nirUpaRaM, kIrtanaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ionship,Ⓒs.ⒹbaMDutA, sanABitA, jYAtiBAvaH, saMbaMDaH; ‘near r(elationship)’ pratyAsannatA; ‘distant r(elationship)’ vyavahitatA.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ive,Ⓒs.ⒹsagotraH, sakulyaH, bAMDavaH, baMDuH, jYAtiH; See Relation.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹsApekza, avivikta, anyasA-pekza, akevala; ‘r(elative) importance’ tAratamyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anyonyAnvita.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 saMbaMDin, vizayaka, in comp.; anuvidDa, anuzakta, saMbadDa, sAnvaya, uddizwa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 saMbaMDavAcin.<BR>Ⓝ[Relat]ively,Ⓒadv.ⒹanyApekzayA, anyasApekzaM, apekzya; See Comparative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.