respond
Respond,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓprativac 2 P, prativad 1 P, uttaraM dA 3 U; See Reply.<BR>Ⓝ[Respond]ent,Ⓒs.ⒹprativAdin m., pratyarTin, uttaravAdin m.<BR>ⓃResponse,Ⓒs.ⒹuttaraM, prativacanaM, prativAkyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 prativAdaH, uttaraM.<BR>ⓃResponsible,Ⓒa.ⒹanuyogADIna, anuyojya, AhvAnA-DIna, prazwavya; oft. by uttaraM dA; ‘you are r(esponsible) for this act’ asya tvayEvottaraM dAtavyaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 DUrvaha, DUrvoQf, DuraMDara, DurIRa.<BR>ⓃResponsibility,Ⓒs.ⒹBAraH, BaraH, Dur f.; ‘the whole r(esponsibility) of the kingdom’ rAjyasya samasto BaraH, rAjyaDurA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anuyo-gADInatA, prazwavyatA.<BR>ⓃResponsive,Ⓒa.ⒹuttaradAyin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMvAdin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rest
Rest,Ⓒv. t.ⒹviSram 4 P, vi-A-ram 1 P, (kAryAt) nivft 1 A; niScalIBU 1 P, sTirIBU, niScezwIBU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Lean against) AlaMb 1 A, upA-samA-A-Sri 1 U; ni-upa-DA pass.; ‘with her face r(est)ing on her; left hand’ vAmahastopahitavadanA (S. 4); oft. by BaraM kf 8 U (with loc.); ‘r(est)ing on his three hoof (legs)’ Kuratraye BaraM kftvA (H. 2); daMqe BAraM niDAya, yazwi-mavalaMbya, &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 pra-upa-Sam 4 P, suKin-nirvfta-svasTa a. BU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 SI 2 A, svap 2 P, saM-viS 6 P, ni-drA 2 P, ni-lI 4 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 sTA 1 P, BU, vft; ‘r(est) with’ avalaMb, apekz 1 A, aDIna-Ayatta a. BU; See Depend (on); ‘further than this r(est)s with fate’ BAgyATattamataH paraM (S. 4).<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹviSram c., SI c., saMviS c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 niviS c., nyas 4 U, avalaMb c., sTA c., A-ni-DA 3 U; cApe vijayASaMsAM nidaDO ‘r(est)ed his hope of victory on his bow’ sakalaripujayASA yatra badDA sutEste (Ve. 5) ‘on whom your sons has r(est)ed their hopes of overthrowing all enemies’.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹviSrA(Sra)maH, viSrAMti f., kArya-vyApAra-nivfttiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Of a body) sTiratA, niScalatA, niScezWatA, acalatA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 suKaM, sOKyaM, svAsTyaM, nirvfti f., pra-upa-SamaH-SAMti f.; See Ease.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 avalaMbanaM, ADAraH, sTAnaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 nidrA, SayanaM, saMveSaH-SanaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 ava-, SezaH-SizwaM; anya, itara, apara (a. pl.) (of persons); Adi, praBfti, in comp.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 yati f., avasAnaM; ‘at r(est)’ niScala, niScezwa, acala, sTira; susTa, pra-upa-SAMta, nirvfta, viSrAMta; nirvyApAra, nirudyoga.<BR>Ⓝ[Rest]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹAlaMbita, ASrita, ni-upa-hita, sTita; sTa, vartin in comp.; ‘r(esting) place’ Sayana-viSrAma-sTAnaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Rest]less,Ⓒa.ⒹvyAkula, paryA-samA-kula, pAriplava, aSAMta, vihvala, asvasTa, vyagra, anirvfta, udvigna.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 capala, caMcala, cala; sadAgati, sAspaMda.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 unnidra, vinidra, nirRidra, ‘passes r(estless) nights’ unnidrA rajanIM gamayati (Mal. 3).<BR>Ⓝ[Rest]lessly,Ⓒadv.ⒹanirvftaM, vyagraM; caMcalatayA.<BR>Ⓝ[Rest]lessness,Ⓒs.ⒹanirvftiH, asvAsTyaM, udvegaH, vyagratA, cApalyaM, cAMcalyaM, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

