restore
Restore,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓpunar-prati-dA 3 U or f c. (arpayati), pratipad c., niryat 10, parAvft c., pratyAnI 1 P; punarlaB 1 A, pratipad 4 A, prAp 5 P, (when passively used) pratyarpitasvAMgaH ‘with his body r(estor)ed to him’; smaraM vapuzA svena niyojayizyati (K. iv. 42) ‘will r(estore) to Cupid his body’; ‘r(estor)ed the universe to the rule of Indra’ punarapi triBuvanamiMdravaSamagAt or nItaM, iMdraSAsanAyattaM kftaM; ‘r(estor)ed to its pristine splendour’ purARaSoBAmaDiropitAyAM (vasatO) (R. xvi. 42), ‘r(estore) to life’ jIv c., socCvAsa a. kf 8 U, asUn prAp c.; ‘r(estor)ed to consciousness’ labDasaMjYa, prAptacEtanyaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Restor]ation,Ⓒs.ⒹpratidAnaM, pratyarpaRaM, pratipAdanaM, niryAtanaM, parAvartanaM, pratyAnayanaM, udDAraH, pUrvAvasTAprApaRaM, &c.<BR>Ⓝ[Restor]ative,Ⓒa.ⒹagnivarDana (nI f.), sattva-bala-varDana^1.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹbalavarDanaM, balyaM, vAjIkaraRaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Restor]er,Ⓒs.ⒹpratidAtf m., pratyarpayitA.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20160822.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrain
Restrain,Ⓒv. t.ⒹsaM-ava-ni-ruD 7 U, nigrah 9 P, ni saM-yam 1 P, ni-prati-baMD 9 P, A-vf 5 U, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=395" target="_blank">Page395</a>] saMhf 1 P, ni-, yaMtr 10; See Forbid, Control also.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Legally) AsiD 1 P, ruD.<BR>Ⓝ[Restrain]er,Ⓒs.ⒹniyaMtf m., nigrahItA, niroDakaH.<BR>ⓃRestraint,Ⓒs.ⒹnigrahaH, ni-ava-roDaH, saM-ni-yamaH, ni-, yaMtraRaM-RA, pratibaMDaH, staMBaH, pratiroDaH, bADA, yamaH, jayaH, damaH (of the senses).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 AseDaH; ‘r(estraint) of a speech’ vAgyamaH, vAksaMyamaH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrict
Restrict,Ⓒv. t.ⒹniruD 7 U, niyaMtr 10, avaDf 10, ni-saM-yam 1 P, nibaMD 9 P, pari-mA 3 A 2 P, nigrah 9 P, ‘my actions being thus r(estrict)ed on all sides’ evaM sarvato nirudDacezwAprasa-rasya me (Mu. 3); bAD 1 A, vyAvft c. (scope) apavAda ivotsargaM vyAvartayitumISvaraH (R. xv. 7) ‘can r(estric) the scope of a rule’.<BR>Ⓝ[Restrict]ed,Ⓒa.Ⓓniyata, samaryAda, sAvaDika, parimita &c.; See Limited.<BR>Ⓝ[Restrict]ion,Ⓒs.ⒹsImA, iyattA, niyamaH, maryAdA, avaDiH, paricCedaH, nibaMDaH, niroDaH, avaDAraRA, vyAvftti f., yaMtraRA; ‘without r(estriction)’ svEraM, yaTecCaM, ani-yaMtraRaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Restrict]ive,Ⓒa.ⒹvyAvartaka, niyAmaka, paricCedaka, avaDAraRa; tuSabdo'vaDAraRArTaH, vyAvfttyarTakaH (S. B.) ‘has a r(estricive) sense’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

result
Result,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓava-paryava-so 4 P, vi-, pari-Ram 1 U; See End.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 utpad-nizpad 4 A, pra-saM-ud-BU 1 P, jan 4 A, pravft 1 A; See Produce; gen. ex. by (s.); ‘it will r(esult) in nothing’ tannirarTakaM Bavet; ‘it will r(esult) in destructing’ tasya nASa eva PalaM Bavet<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹpariRAmaH, PalaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 arTaH, guRaH, nizpannaM, sidDi f.; aMtaH, avasAnaM, SevaH, udarkaH; pAkaH; ‘good r(esult)’ SuBaPalaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 sidDAMtaH, maTitArTaH, niScitArTaH; ‘producing no r(esult)’ nizPala, nirguRa, vyarTa.<BR>Ⓝ[Result]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓja, janya, udBava, Pala in comp.; See Produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resume
Resume,Ⓒv. t.ⒹpunaH-BUyaH-AdA 3 A or grah 9 U or Ap 5 P or laB 1 A, pratyAhf 1 P; ‘let us r(esume) (the thread of) our discourse’ prakftaM-prastutavizayaM-anusaMdaDAma or anusarAma; oft. by punaH-BUyaH-AraB 1 A or kf, with other words; ‘r(esum)ed their fighting’ punaryodDumAreBire, ataH paraM punaH kaTayizyAmi (M. 4) ‘I shall r(esume) my story from this point afterwards’; ‘he r(esum)ed his discourse’ punarvaktuM pracakrame.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹsAraH, saMgrahaH, sArArTaH<BR>ⓃResumption,Ⓒs.ⒹpratyAdAnaM, punargrahaRaM, pratyAhAraH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

