sacrifice
Sacrifice,Ⓒs.ⒹyajYaH; kratuH, aDvaraH, yAgaH, ijyA, maKaH, savaH, homaH, havanaM, izwi f., meDaH in comp.; ‘horse-s(acrifice)’ aSvameDaH; ‘human s(acrifice)’ narameDaH-yajYaH &c.; ‘imperial s(acrifice)’ rAjasUyaH; ‘fit for a s(acrifice)’ yajYiya, meDya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 AlaMBaH, utsargaH, baliH, upahAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 vyayaH, utsargaH, pari-, tyAgaH, viniyogaH, samarpaRaM; ‘even at the s(acrifice) of oneʼs life’ jIvitavyayenApi, prARaparityAgenApi; oft. by instr. alone (AtmAnaM satataM rakzet dArErapi DanErapi).<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓyaj 1 U; hu 3 U, upahf 1 P, utsargArTaM han 2 P or baliM dA 3 U, samA-A laB 1 A (animal); ‘he s(acrifice)s a beast to Rudra’ paSunA rudraM yajate; ‘he s(acrific)ed a horse’ aSvameDaM tatAna, aSva-meDena Ije.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pari-tyaj 1 P, ut-sfj 6 P, hA 3 P, saM-f c. (arpayati), viniyuj 7 A, 10; ‘s(acrific)ing their own interests’ svArTaM parityajya; ‘without s(acrific)ing their interest’ svArTAviroDena (Bh. i. 74).<BR>Ⓝ[Sacrific]er,Ⓒs.ⒹyajamAnaH, yazwf m., yAjakaH, yajvan m., yAjYikaH, hotf m.<BR>ⓃSacrificial,Ⓒa.ⒹyajYiya, vEtAna (nI f.), meDya; yajYa in comp.; ‘s(acrificial) work’ yajYakarma; ‘s(acrificial) fire’ homAgniH, samUhyaH, pari-cAyyaH, upacAyyaH; ‘s(acrificial) priest’ ftvij m.; See Priest; ‘s(acrificial) session’ satraM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

