semblance
Semblance,Ⓒs.ⒹABAsaH, ABA, OpamyaM, sAdfSyaM; AkAraH, rUpaM; ‘it has a s(emblance) of truth’ satyamivAvaBAsate, satyasaMkASaM; ‘to wear the s(emblance) of displeasure (anger)’ kftakakopaM darSayituM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

