sense
Sense,Ⓒs.ⒹiMdriyaM, hfzIkaM, vizayin n., ‘s(ense)s collectively’ iMdriyavargaH-gaRaH, paMceMdriyaM; ‘s(ense)s of perception or knowledge’ jYAneMdriyARi; ‘s(ense)s of action’ karmeMdri-yARi, karaRAni, karmasADanAni; ‘evident to the s(ense)’ pratyakza, iMdriya-grAhya-gocara; ‘pleasures of s(ense)’ vizaya-iMdriya-suKaM, ‘object of s(ense)’ vizayaH, iMdriyArTaH, iMdriya-vizayaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 upalabDi f., vedanaM-nA, boDaH, jYAnaM, anuboDaH, grahaRaM, saMvedanaM, iMdriyaboDaH-grahaRaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 budDi f., mati f., DIH, cicCaktiH, prajYA; See Intellect.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 cetanA, saMjYA, cEtanyaM; jYAnaM, boDaH, anuBavaH, saMvedanaM; ‘s(ense) of obligation’ kftajYatA, kftaveditvaM; ‘s(ense) of pleasure’ suKaboDaH-anuBavaH; ‘come to s(ense)s’, ‘recover oneʼs s(ense)s’ saMjYAM-cetanAM-laB 1 A or A-prati-pad 4 A, prakftiM A-pad, prakftisTa a. BU 1 P; ‘loss of s(ense)s’ mati-BraMSaH, budDi-mati-nASaH, viplavaH; ‘common s(ense)’ vivekaH; ‘good s(ense)’ subudDiH, sadBAvaH; sOjanyaM; ‘out of s(ense)s’ vigatacetana, lupta-saMjYa, nazwa-hata-jYAna, budDiBrazwa, nazweMdriya-budDi; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=417" target="_blank">Page417</a>] ‘who has lost all s(ense) of honour and dishonour on account of old age’ jarAvaluptamAnAvamAnacittaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 mataM, aBiprAyaH, uddeSaH, ASayaH, AkAMkzA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 arTaH, BAvaH (purport); ‘understanding the literal s(ense)’ SAbdaboDaH; ‘literal s(ense)’ SabdArTaH; akzarArTaH; ‘in its true s(ense)’ anvarTa-yaTArTa.<BR>Ⓔa.ⒹyaTArTataH, paramArTataH, arTataH; ‘else this repetition has no s(ense)’ anyaTA ezA vIpsA na caritArTA Bavati (Ka. 320), nirarTakA Bavet &c.; See Significant.<BR>Ⓝ[Sens]ible,Ⓒa.ⒹiMdriyagocara-grAhya-gamya-jYeya, pratyakza.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vizaya-iMdriyArTa-grAhin, grahaRa-samarTa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 aBijYa, jYa, vedin in comp.; ‘s(ensible) of your service’ tvatsevABijYa; upakArajYa-vedin ‘s(ensible) of obligations’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 saMjYAvat, cetanopapanna, sacetana, cetana, cetanAvat, vedana-jYAna-kzama; labDa or prApta-saMjYa or cEtanya, Apanna-cetana.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 mati-budDi-mat, sajYAna, jYAnavat, vivekin, jYAna-budDi-SAlin, manasvin, DIsaMpanna; See Rational also.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 vicakzaRa, suDI, sumeDas, prAjYa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 upapanna, yukta, ucita, saMgata, samaMjasa, sayuktika, yuktipUrva.<BR>Ⓝ[Sens]ibility,Ⓒs.ⒹgrahaRasAmarTyaM-Sakti f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sUkzma or SIGra-cEtanyaM or boDaH; vedanaM-nA, boDaH, jYAnaM, anuBavaH, cetanA; cEtanyaM; saMjYA.<BR>Ⓝ[Sens]ibly,Ⓒadv.ⒹpratyakzaM-kzataH, &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 subudDyA, subudDipUrvaM, boDa-jYAna-pUrvaM, cetanavat, aBrameRa.<BR>Ⓝ[Sense]less,Ⓒa.Ⓓacetana, vizayagrahaRAkzama.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 a-vi-gata-cetana, niHsaMjYa, luptasaMjYa, nazwacEtanya, suptabudDi, saMjYA-cEtanya-hIna.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 durbudDi, mati-budDi-hIna, mUQa, mUrKa, anAtmajYa, nirboDa; See Foolish.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 ayukta, asamaMjasa, anupapanna, anucita.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 nirarTaka, asaMgata, asaMbadDa.<BR>Ⓝ[Sense]lessly,Ⓒadv.ⒹmUrKavat, mUQavat, &c.<BR>ⓃSensitive,Ⓒa.Ⓓsacetana, cetanAvat, vizayagrahaRakzama-samarTa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 sUkzma or SIGra or vedin or grAhin, SIGracetana; caleMdriya, anAyAsena saMkzoBya, mfduprakfti, komalahfdaya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 lajjAlu, lajjAvat; See Modest; ‘s(ensitive) plant’ lajjAluH, namaskArin m.<BR>Ⓝ[Sensitive]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹSIGrajYAnena, sUkzmacEtanyena.<BR>Ⓝ[Sensitive]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹsUkzmacEtanyaM, SIGraboDaH, &c.<BR>ⓃSensual,Ⓒa.ⒹiMdriya, vizaya in comp.; ‘s(ensual) pleasures’ vizayasuKAni, iMdriyopaBogaH, vizayAsakti f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Of persons) iMdriyasuKanirata, vizayA-sakta, vizayaparAyaRa-para-nirata-aDIna-vaSa, iMdriyavaSa, &c.; vizayin, viza-yopasevin, vizayasuKAsakta, Boga-kAma-Asakta.<BR>Ⓝ[Sensual]ist,Ⓒs.Ⓓvizayin m., vizayAsaktaH, BogAsaktaH; See above.<BR>Ⓝ[Sensual]ity, [Sensual]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹvizayAsaktiH, iMdriyasuKopaBogaH, vizaya-vaSatA-parAyaRatA &c., BogAsaktiH, kAmA-saktiH, iMdriya-vizaya-suKaniratiH.<BR>ⓃSentient,Ⓒa.Ⓓsacetas, sacetana, cetanAvat, cEtanya-prARa-viSizwa; See Sensible; ‘a s(entient) being’ prARin m., dehin m., SarIrin m. jIvaH, prARaBft m., cetanaH.<BR>ⓃSensation,Ⓒs.ⒹpratyakzaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saM-vedanaM-nA, boDaH, jYAnaM, upalabDiH, cetanA, pratyakzajYAnaM, anuBavaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 vikAraH, vi-kriyA; ‘produced a great s(ensation) among the people’ janamanAMsi BfSaM samakzoBayat-Aku-lIcakAra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

