sentence
Sentence,Ⓒs.ⒹnirRayaH, daMqAjYA, daMqAdeSaH, ADarzaRaM; ‘s(entence) of death’ prARadaMqAjYA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vicAraH, niScayaH, nirRayaH, saMkalpaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 vAkyaM, vacanaM, ukti f., vacas n., padasamUhaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 sUtraM.<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹdaMqaM AdiS 6 P or nirRI 1 P or kaT 10 or nivid c.; ‘s(eiz)ed him to death’ tasya vaDadaMqamAdiSat, vaDyatAmasO iti AjYApayat.<BR>ⓃSententious,Ⓒa.ⒹlAGavayukta, lAGavaguRopeta, sUtramaya (yI f.), sUtraprAya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentiment
Sentiment,Ⓒs.ⒹmataM, aBiprAyaH, budDi f., mati f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saMkalpaH, kalpanA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 arTaH; See Sense, Idea.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 BAvaH, rasaH, rAgaH; ‘s(entiment) of love’ SfMgArarasaH; karuRArasaH; &c.<BR>Ⓝ[Sentiment]al,Ⓒa.Ⓓrasika, rasamaya (yI f.), sarasa, rasAtmaka, sarAga, rasaBUyizWa.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kAlpanika (kI f.), BAvita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

