separate
Separate,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓviyuj 7 A, 10, vi-, rah 1 P, 10 (rahayati), vinAkf 8 U, (with instr.); ‘Rati s(eperat)ed from Madana’ madanena vi-nAkftA ratiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pfTak kf, viSliz c., vi-, Bid 7 P or c. viBaj 1 U, vicCid 7 P, viGaw c., vigam c. (gamayati); vyAsaMj c., vyatiric 7 P or c.; (distinguish between) vivic 3, 7 U, viSiz 7 P or c.; ‘s(eparat)ing milk from water’ dugDajala-BedaviDiH.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹpfTagBU 1 P, viSliz 4 P, viGaw 1 A, apayA 2 P, vyapa-i 2 P, viyuj-vicCid-Bid- pass.; ‘the brothers have s(eperat)ed’ viBaktA BrAtaraH.<BR>Ⓝ[Separat]ed,Ⓒa.Ⓓvi-, Binna, viBakta, viyukta, vicCinna; na jAne kiyatADvanA vicCinnamito balamanuyAyi me (Ka. 120) ‘by what distance s(eparted)’ &c.; pfTak ind., asaMlagna, asaMsfzwa, vyatirikta, vyasta.<BR>Ⓝ[Separat]ion,Ⓒs.ⒹviyogaH, virahaH, viprayogaH, viSlezaH, viBedaH, vyatirekaH, vicCedaH, (with instr. for ‘from’); BinnatA, pArTakyaM, pfTagBAvaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pfTakkaraRaM, viBAgaH, vi-, BedaH-danaM, vyAsaMgaH, vigamaH, viGawanaM; vivekaH; ‘afflicted by s(eparation)’ virahAtura, virahaparyutsuka, viDura.<BR>Ⓝ[Separate]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹpfTak, vi-, BinnaM; ‘taken s(eparately)’ ekEka a.; vyasta a. sarvAvinayAnAmekEkamapyezAmAyatanaM (Ka. 103), tadasti kiM vyastamapi trilo-cane (K. v. 72) ‘even one, taken s(eparately)’ &c.<BR>Ⓝ[Separate]ness,Ⓒs.ⒹpfTagBAvaH, pArTakyaM. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=418" target="_blank">Page418</a>]<BR>ⓃSeparable,Ⓒa.ⒹviBAjya, viyojya, vicCedya; ‘not s(eparable)’ nityasTAyin, nitya, prakftisTa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

