serve
Serve,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓsev 1 A, Sru desid. (SuSrUzate) upAs 1 A, upasTA 1 A, upacar 1 P, pari-anu-car; ‘he who s(erve)s not anotherʼs will’ parecCAnurUpaM na vartate, paracCedAnuvartI na Bavati, anyaBAvaM na anupraviSati.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anu-vft 1 A, anuruD 4 A, anuvi-DA 3 U; See Obey.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 upakf 8 U, anugrah 9 P, upacar, sAhAyyaM kf; SreyaH-saM-pad c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 (arTaM) sAD c., pravft c., saM-pad c., nirvft c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 paryApta-ucita a. BU 1 P, alaM with dat. or inf., kxp 1 A (with dat.); ‘this will s(erve) to rouse his anger’ tasya kopamuddIpayitu-kopoddIpanAya-alaM or paryAptamidaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 upa-pari-kxp c., upasTA c. (sTApayati).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 sTAne-BUmO-vft or BU or prayuj pass.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 pra-upa-yuj 7 U, 10, vini-yuj, nikzip 6 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		9 vft; Acar, vyava-hf 1 P, (with loc. of person); See Act, Behave; ‘s(erve) the purpose of’, ‘s(erve) as’ upayogaM vraj 1 P, sTAne-BUmO-BU; BUrja-tvacaH vrajaMti vidyADarasuMdarIRAmanaMgaleKakriya yopayogaM (K. i. 7) ‘s(erve) as love-letters’ &c.; ‘s(erve) up meals’ pariviz c., annaM upasTA c.; ‘the Gods s(erv)ed up food’ marutaH parivezwAraH Asan; ‘s(erve) out’ pratikf, vEraM &c. niryat 10.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹsevAM-kAryaM-kf; niyo-gamanuzWA 1 P; kAryaM saMpad c.; ‘this will s(erve) as water to wash his feet with’ idaM pAdodakaM Bavizyati (S. 1).<BR>Ⓝ[Serv]ant,Ⓒs.ⒹBftyaH, sevakaH, kiMkaraH, anu-upa-jIvin m., dAsaH, cewaH, prezyaH, anu-pari-caraH, parijanaH, paricArakaH, niyojyaH, BujizyaH, SuSrUzakaH, upAsakaH, sevAjIvin m., vEtanikaH, BftiBuj m., BaraRyaBuj m., BftakaH; karmaka(kA)raH, (labourer); ‘female s(ervant)’, ‘s(ervant)-maid’ cewI, dAsI, BujizyA, prezyA, karmakarI, sEraM(riM)DrI.<BR>ⓃService,Ⓒs.ⒹsevA, SuSrUzA, upacAraH, upa-pari-caryA, upAsanaM-nA; A-saM-SryaH; ‘s(ervice) of kings’ nfpasaMSrayaH, rAjASrayaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (State) dAsyaM, dAsavftti f., prezya-Bftya-BAvaH, sevA; ‘he lives in my s(ervice)’ sa mAmanujIvati madASritaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 anuvartanaM, anuvfttiH, ArADanaM; See Obedience.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 vfttiH, niyogaH, kAryaM, vyavasAyaH; vyApAraH, karman n., vyavahAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 upakAraH, sAhAyyaM, upakftaM-ti f., anugrahaH, hitaM, arTaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 upayogaH, vyavahAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 saparyA, upAsanA, pUjA, upacAraH, pUjopacAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=419" target="_blank">Page419</a>] BojanapAtragaRaH; ‘I am entirely at your s(ervice)’ sarvaTA tvadaDInohaM, BavatA yaTecCaM niyujyatAmayaM dAsaH; ‘in whose s(ervice) are you’ kasya sevayA jIvasi, kena niyuktastvaM; ‘to keep in s(ervice)’ sevAyAM niyuj 7 U, 10, (karmaRi) vyApf c.<BR>Ⓝ[Servic]able,Ⓒa.Ⓓupayukta; upayogin, upakArin, sahAyaBUta, pra-upa-yojya.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kAryakzama, karmakuSala, alaMkarmIRa.<BR>Ⓝ[Servic]ably,Ⓒadv.ⒹsopayogaM, salABaM, so-pakAraM.<BR>ⓃServile,Ⓒa.ⒹdAseya (yI f.), dA-socita, dAsa-dAsya in comp.; ‘s(ervile) state’ dAsaBAvaH, dAsyaM, prezyaBAvaH, dAsyavfttiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aticAwupara, atyanuroDin, Svavftti, ati-lAlanapara.<BR>Ⓝ[Servil]ity,Ⓒs.ⒹdAsyaM, dAsyaBAvaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 caraRAvapAtaH, SvavfttiH, atilAlanaM, atyanu-roDaH, CaMdonuvartanaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Servile]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹdAsavat, atya-nuroDena, atilAlanapUrvaM^1.<BR>ⓃServitor,Ⓒs.Ⓓse-vakaH, BftyaH, &c.; See Servant.<BR>ⓃServitude,Ⓒs.ⒹdAsyaM, BftyaBAvaH, kiMkaratvaM, sevA, prezyaBAvaH, SvavfttiH, sevADarmaH, sevaka-daSA.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

