settle
Settle,Ⓒv. t.ⒹsTA c. (sTApayati), prati-ava-°, ni-A-ruh c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 saM-vyava-sTA c., vyavaso 4 P, nir-ava-Df 10, saMkxp c., sAD c.; ‘s(ettl)ing what to say’ vyavasTApitavAk, vAcaM vyavasTApya; asyAH pituH samIpanayanamavasTitameva (S. 5) ‘is but s(ettl)ed &c.’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Lands &c.) dA 3 U, yuj 10 (with instr. of grant); tvAM SAsanaSatena yojayizyAmi (P. i. 4).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 aDivas c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 sTirIkf 8 U, svasTanirvfta a. kf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 pra-, Sam c. (Samayati), saM-DA 3 U, samA-DA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 saM-, vi-DA, vi-, rac, vinyas 4 U; ‘s(ettle) in marriage’ niviS c., (tanayaM niveSya S. 4); ‘s(ettle) a debt’ fRaM SuD c. or apAkf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 aDaH pat c. or gam c., ava-sad c.<BR>Ⓔv. i.Ⓓava-vyava-sTA 1 A, sTirIBU 1 P, nivAsaM sTirIkf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 praSam 4 P, viSram 4 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 tale pat 1 P, sad 1 P, ava-ni-°, aDaH gam 1 P; prasad (for becoming clear).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 aDaH pat c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 GanIBU, saMhan pass., saMhatIBU; ‘s(ettl)ed amongst themselves’ miTaH praSamaM yAtAH, parasparasaMDAnamakurvan; ‘s(ettle) in life’ vivah pass., niviS 6 A (saMsArapaTaM), vivAhaM kf, pratizWita a. BU.<BR>Ⓝ[Settl]ed,Ⓒa.ⒹsTApita, ropita, pratizWita &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 niyata, niScita, nirRIta, vyavasTita, sidDa, nizpanna.<BR>Ⓝ[Settl]ing, [Settle]ment,Ⓒs.ⒹsTApanaM, saM-prati-ava-°.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 nirRayaH, niScayaH, nirDAraRaM-RA, avaDAraRaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 saM-DAnaM, pra-, SamaH-manaM, saMDiH, samADAnaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 aDivAsanaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 aDivAsitadeSaH; ‘s(ettling) in life’ vivAhaH, saMsAra-pratizWA; ‘marriage-s(ettlement)’ SulkaH-lkaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Settl]er,Ⓒs.ⒹaDivAsin m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

