shake
Shake,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓpra-, kaMp-vep- 1 A, vi-pra-cal 1 P, vell 1 P, saM-pra-kzuB 4 P, 1 A; (fig.) aBiBU-bAD- pass.<BR>Ⓔv. t.ⒹkaMp c., DU 5, 9 U, 6 P, vi-A-°, cal c., saM-vi-pra°; kzuB c.; DvAnena sarvataH pracalitamiva tadaraRyaBavet (Ka. 29) ‘was, as if, s(hak)en by the sound’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 aBiBU 1 P, AkulIkf 8 U; ‘this position would be s(hak)en’ iti pratipAditamAkulIBavet (S. B. 335); ‘s(hake) oneʼs confidence’ sASaMka-SaMkAnvita a. kf; ‘s(hake) about’ preMK c., AMdolayati (D.); ‘s(hake) off’ nirDU, niras 4 U, nirAkf, apAs, tyaj 1 P, apAnud 6 P, pratisf c.; See Dispel; ‘s(hake) hands with each other’ anyonyaM hastO spfSataH.<BR>Ⓝ[Shak]ing,Ⓒs.ⒹkaMpaH, DUnanaM, vi-, Du(DU)ti f., vicalanaM, vepanaM, saM-, kzoBaH.<BR>Ⓔa.Ⓓcala, sakaMpa, calana, lola, tarala, caMcala, pAriplava.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 kzoBakArin.<BR>Ⓝ[Shak]y,Ⓒa.ⒹasTira, cala, lola; See Fickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

