share
Share,Ⓒv. t.ⒹsaM-viBaj 1 U, parikxp c., aMS 10, vaMw 10; aMSAMSi dA 3 U; ‘sorrow s(har)ed by dear friends’ snigDajanasaMviBaktaM duHKaM-^1 (S. 3); ‘with whom else shall I s(hare) my grief’ kena vAnyena saha sADAraRIkaromi duHKaM (Ka. 233).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 BAgaM-aMSaM-hf 1 P or laB 1 A or grah 9 U, anyena saha Buj 7 A; ‘the demons shall s(hare) the labour of churning’ dAnavA api maMTanaSramaBAjaH BaveyuH, (yuzmABiH sArDaM) maMTanaSramamanuBaveyuH, &c.; ‘s(har)ing equally pleasure and pain’ samaduHKasuKa.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹaMSaH, BAgaH, vaMwaH, udDAraH (of an estate); ‘he is to have a s(hare)’ aMSaBAgBavet; ‘he has a s(hare) in the plot’ kapawaprabaMDe sahakArI asO.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (Of a plough) PAlaH kuSI.<BR>Ⓝ[Shar]er,Ⓒs.ⒹaMSaharaH, aMSin m., BAgin-BAk in comp.<BR>ⓃShare-holder,Ⓒs.ⒹaMSaBAgI, aMSagrAhI, BAgahArI-grAhI.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

