spirit
Spirit,Ⓒs.ⒹprARAH, asavaH, (pl.).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 Atman m., dehin m., kzetrajYaH; See Soul; ‘the supreme s(pirit)’ paramAtmA, brahma.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 cittaM, manas-cetas n., vftti f., BAvaH; ‘low-s(pirit)ed’ laGucetas, kzudramanas ‘proudness of s(pirit)’ cittasamunnati f., cittodrekaH; See Pride; ‘in good s(pirit)s’, ‘in high s(pirit)s’ sollAsa, prahfzwa, pramudita-citta; harzavftti; ‘high s(pirit)s’ utsAhaH, u-llAsaH, praPullatA, praharzaH; ‘low s(pirit)s’, vizAdaH, udvegaH; ‘in low s(pirit)s’ udvigna, vizaRRa, udAsIna; See Dejected.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 sattvaM, tejas n., vIryaM, praBAvaH, UrjaH, utsAhaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 BAvaH, BAvArTaH, uddeSaH; ‘he obeyed my order in s(pirit) only’ BAvArTameva gfhItvA mamAjYAmanuzWitavAn.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 sAraH, tattvaM, sattvaM, sA-rAMSaH, jIvitaM; jIvanaM; ‘Ojas is the s(pirit) (soul) of prose’ ojaH gadyasya jIvitaM (Kav.).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 prakfti f., SIlaM, svaBAvaH, vfttiH; ‘gentle s(pirit)’ svaBAvasOjanyaM, SAMtaSIlatA; ‘of a noble s(pirit)’ udAraprakfti.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 BUtaH, vetAlaH; ‘evil s(pirit)’ rakzas n., rAkzasaH, piSAcaH, apa-devatA,<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		9 pretaH, paretaH, CAyA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		10 (Of style) ojas n., UrjaH; rasaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		11 (‘S(pirit)s’) surA, madyaM; See Liquor.<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓ(up) ASvas c., ujjIv c., uttij c.<BR>Ⓝ[Spirit]ed,Ⓒa.Ⓓsattvavat, sotsAha, tejasvin, vIryavat, sattva; ‘a s(pirited) speech’ UrjitASrayaM vacanaM.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 ojasvin, sarasa.<BR>Ⓝ[Spirit]edly,Ⓒadv.ⒹsotsAhaM, sasattvaM.<BR>Ⓝ[Spirit]less,Ⓒa.ⒹniHsattva, tejovihIna; nistejas, nirvIrya, nIrasa.<BR>Ⓝ[Spirit]uous,Ⓒa.ⒹmAdin, mAdaka; ‘s(pirituous) liquor’ surA, madirA, &c.<BR>ⓃSpiritual,Ⓒa.ⒹaDyAtma in comp., (aDyAtmajYAnaM), A-DyAtmika (kI f.); niravayava, nirAkAra, cidrUpa, amUrta, parama.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pAratrika-pAralOkika-pAramArTika (kI f.), mAnasika-sAttvika- (kI f.),<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 DArmika (kI f.), Darma in comp.; asAMsArika-alOkika- (kI f.); ‘s(piritual) preceptor’ upADyAyaH; ‘s(piritual) father’ DarmatAtaH-pitf m.<BR>Ⓝ[Spiritual]ism,Ⓒs.ⒹbrahmavAdaH, jYAna-nivftti-mArgaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Spiritual]ist,Ⓒs.ⒹbrahmavAdin m.<BR>Ⓝ[Spiritual]ity,ⒶamUrtatA, asAMsArikatA, paramArTanizWA.<BR>Ⓝ[Spiritual]ly,Ⓒadv.ⒹparamArTadfzwyA, paramArTataH; ‘s(piritually) minded’ paramArTadfzwi-budDi, paramArTAsakta, brahmanizWa saMsAravyAvftta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

