take
Take,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓgrah 9 U, prati-pari-° (in all senses) agfhIte rAkzase (Mu. 1); upa-deSaM gfhARa &c.; A-dA 3 A, prati-iz 6 P; svI-aMgI-kf 8 U.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 Df 1 P, 10, A-ava-laMb 1 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (A word in a sense) pari-, grah; tatrATaSabda AnaMtaryArTaH parigfhyate (S. B. 23) ‘is taken in the sense of’ &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 nI 1 P, vah 1 P, hf 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 upalaB 1 A, avagam 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 anuBU 1 P; See Suffer, Affect.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 laB, prAp 5 P, aDigam, A-sad c.; See Get.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 Captivate, q. v.; ‘t(ake) food’ AhAraM sev 1 A; ‘t(ake) the field’ raRa-BUmiM avatF 1 P, raRAMgaRe yuD 4 A; ‘t(ake) rest’ viSram 4 P; ‘t(ake) root’ mUlaM baMD 9 P; ‘t(ake) heart’ samASvas 2 P, DEryaM avalaMb-avazwaMB 9 P; See Courage; ‘t(ake) fire’ dah pass., agniM upa-i 2 P; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=462" target="_blank">Page462</a>] ‘t(ake) in hand’ pratipad 4 A, u(U)rIkf ‘t(ake) place’; See Happen; ‘t(ake) part in’ hastaM dA 3 U, saMgin-sahakArin-sahAya a. BU; ‘took part in the massacre’ viSa-sane sahAyo baBUva; ‘t(ake) aim’ saM-DA 3 U; ‘t(ake) oneʼs way’ siD-sAD c. (sADayati), sADayAmo vayaM (S. 1); ‘t(ake) effect’ Pal 1 P, saPalIBU 1 P; ‘t(ake) possession of’ Akram 1 U, 4 P, AviS 6 P; ‘t(ake) to task’ nirBarts 10 A, paruzaM niMd 1 P.<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹsiD 4 P, saMpad 4 A, guRaM Avah.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 ASri 1 U, vraj 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] away,Ⓐapa-vi-nI 1 P, apa-, hf 1 P, apa-Uh 1 U, vinud c.; See Remove.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] back,ⒶsaM-pratisaM-hf, pratyA-dA, pratyAnI.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] down,Ⓐavaruh c., ni-ava-pat c., aDo nI.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 liK 6 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] for,Ⓐman 4 A; See Consider; ‘mischievousness is t(ak)en for assiduity’ cApalpamudyogitAM Bajate.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] in,Ⓐgrah, sev; (in the stomach) gras 1 A; ni, ga 6 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 vipra-laB 1 A; See Cheat.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] off,ⒶapanI, avatF c., unmuc 6 P, avakfz.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] out,ⒶbahirnI, apanI.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] to,Ⓐsev, ASri, avalaMb.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] up,Ⓐpratipad, aMgI-svI-kf.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 AraB 1 A, pravft c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 Occupy, Engross, q. v.<BR>Ⓝ[Take] upon (oneself),ⒶaMgIkf, pratipad, u(U)rIkf; (nirvAhaH pratipannavastuzu Mu. 2).<BR>Ⓝ[Tak]er,Ⓒs.ⒹgrahItf m., grAhin-hArin-hft in comp.<BR>Ⓝ[Tak]ing,Ⓒa.Ⓓmohin, manohArin, cittAkarzin, manojYa; See Charming.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 grAhin, &c.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹA-dAnaM, grahaRaM, svIkAraH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

