Throw,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓpra-, kzip 6 P, pra-, as 4 P, pat c., pra-, muc 6 P, visfj 6 P, Ir c. prez c., (with loc. of place); ‘t(hrow) a glance’ dfzwiM-cakzuH-kzip or dA 3 U or pat c.; ‘t(hrow) into disorder’ piMjalI-AkulI-kf 8 U, vyUhaM BaMj 7 P; ‘t(hrow) dice’ akzAn Avap 1 P or pat c.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] about,Ⓐut-vi-kzip, ita-stataH cal c.; bAhUtkzepaM ‘t(hrow)ing about the arms’.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] away,ⒶniH-vi-kzip, apAs, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=469" target="_blank">Page469</a>] apa-hA 3 P, apavyaD 4 P, tyaj 1 P; (time) kzip, hf 1 P, yA^1 c. (yApayati^2).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 niras, pratyAKyA 2 P; See Reject; ‘it was t(hrow)ing words away’ nirarTakaM-moGaM-eva tad BAzaRaM, vAgAyAsamAtrakaM BAzaRaM; ‘kindness was not thrown away upon him’ sonugrahaM kftajYatayAsmarat; ‘to be thrown away upon’ viPalIBU 1 P, viPalatAM gam 1 P, layaM-kzayaM-nASaM-gam-yA &c.; gatA nASaM tArA upakftamasADAviva jane (Mr. 5); asatpuruzaseveva dfzwirviPalatAM gatA (Mr. 1).<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] down,Ⓐpat c., aDaH kzip or pat; pra-BraMS c., pracyu c.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] offⒶniH-pra-kzip, ava-nir-DU 5, 9 U, nirAkf, apavyaD, apa-sf c.; ‘t(hrow) one off his guard’ asAvaDAna a. kf; ‘t(hrow) off the veil or mask’ svarUpaM prakawIkf or vi-vf 5 U or prakAS c.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] out,ⒶReject, q. v.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 niH-, sf c., apAs.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (Hints) sUc 10, upa-kzip, upanyas, vyaMj c.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw] up,Ⓐudas, utkzip &c.; (from the stomach) udvam 1 P, ud-gF 6 P; ‘I have thrown a wall around’ upakzipto mayA BittibaMDaH (M. 5).<BR>Ⓔs.Ⓓpra-, kzepaH-paRaM, prAsanaM, preraRaM; &c.<BR>Ⓝ[Throw]er,Ⓒs.Ⓓkzeptf m., prAsakaH.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161211.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20161211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

