turn
Turn,Ⓒv. i.Ⓓpari-, Bram 1, 4 P, GUrR 1 A, 6 P, vyA-pari-vft 1 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 parivft; oft. by BU 1 P; jan 4 A.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 amlIBU, amlatAM gam 1 P; ‘food t(urn)s into blood’ annaM ruDira-BAvena pariRamati; See Change; ‘t(urn) into white’ SvetIBavati; ‘t(urn) to nothing’ nirarTaka-vyarTa a. BU. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=478" target="_blank">Page478</a>]<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 BU with saMmuKa-aBimuKa- (KI f.) in comp. or with gen.; ‘t(urn)ing to the hero’ nAyakABimuKI BUtvA.<BR>Ⓔv. t.Ⓓpari-, Bram c., (fig. also) GUrR c.; pari-vi-vyA-vft c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 parivft c., A-, vel c., (Ava-litavadanaM rAjakamAsIt Ka. 10); parivfttArDamuKI (V. 1) ‘with her face half-t(urn)ed’.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 viparyas c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 sAcIkf 8 U; See Bend.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 amlIkf; ‘t(urn) to account’; See under Account; ‘t(urn) to use’ upayuj 10; ‘t(urn) into ashes’ BasmasAt-BasmI-kf or BU; ‘t(urn) the back’ pfzWaM dfS c., parANmuKIBU ‘t(urn)s a single fault to two’ ekAparADaM dviguRIkaroti.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] about,Ⓐvi-pari-vft; pari-kram 1 U, 4 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] against,ⒶpratIpayati (D.); (v. i.) pratikUlIBU, pratyarTin a. BU, virudDa a. BU.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] away,ⒶapanI 1 P, dUrIkf; apAs, niHsf c., nirAkf; See Dismiss, Discharge.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 (aside) ni vyAvft c., saM-hf 1 P; sAcIkf, tiryag-val; (aBimuKe mayi saMhftamIkzitaM S. 2); ‘shall t(urn) away his mind’ (in another direction) anyataH enaM kzipAmi-saMcArayAmi; (v. i.) vyAvft 1 A, (vyAvartamAnA hriyA), parANgamuKI vimuKI-BU; muKaM parivft.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] back,Ⓐpari-parA-vft; (v. t.) pari-parA-vft c.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] into,Ⓐkf, (tapovanamupanaM kftaM S. 2).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 pariRam^1 c. with BAvena; AKuM biqAlaBAvena paryaRamayat ‘t(urn)ed the rat into a cat’; See Change.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] off,ⒶdUrIkf, nivft c., apAs &c.; (v. i.) apa-sf 1 P, nirgam 1 P.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] out,Ⓒ(v. t.)ⒹniHsf c., nizkas c., bahizkf; See Discharge.<BR>Ⓔ(v. i.)ⒹsaMpat 1 P; See Happen.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 jan 4 A, BU 1 P; ‘t(urn)ed out pale’ vivarRI-BUtaH, sahasA vivarRaBAvaM prapede; ‘the words of the great never t(urn) out untrue’ na hISvaravyAhftayaH kadAcitpuzRaMti loke viparI-tamarTaM (K. iii. 63).<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] over,Ⓐutkzip 6 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 parivft c., cal c.; ‘t(urn)ing over the pages’ pfzWAni cAlayitvA-samAlokya.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] round,Ⓐpari-parA-vft.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] to,ⒶdfS 1 P, Ikz 1 A; by prati with acc.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] towards,ⒶaBimuKI-saMmuKI-BU (with gen.).<BR>Ⓝ[Turn] up,ⒶsahasA AvirBU or prAdurBU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 Happen, q. v.<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹAvartaH-rtanaM, Avftti f.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 parivfttiH, parivartaH, vikaraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 paryAyaH, parivfttiH; ‘by t(urn)s’ paryAyeRa, paryAya in comp.; ‘service by t(urn)s’ paryAyasevA.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		4 vAraH, (SaSakasya vAraH samAyAtaH P. i. 8).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		5 pra-, vfttiH, BAvaH, daSA; ‘t(urn) of mind’ cittavfttiH, manaHsvaBAvaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		6 AkAraH, svarUpaM; ‘matters took a different t(urn)’ vastu-sTiteravasTAMtaraM adfSyata, sakalo'rTaH parivfttaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		7 gati f., kramaH; ‘mysterious is the t(urn) of fate’ karmaRo gahanA gatiH; ‘t(urn) of fortune’ dEvagatiH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		8 parikramaH; (walk) IzadvihAraH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		9 avasaraH, samayaH, kAlaH.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		10 vaMkaH (of rivers); ‘a good t(urn)’ upakAraH, ‘ill t(urn)’ apakAraH; ‘one good t(urn) deserves another’ upakAraH pratyupakAreRa niryAta-yitavyaH.<BR>Ⓝ[Turn]er,Ⓒs.Ⓓcakrin m., kuMdin m.<BR>ⓃTurncoat,Ⓒs.ⒹsvapakzatyAgin m., samayA-nanuroDin.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

