Yield,Ⓒv. t.Ⓓpra-, dA 1 P, 3 U; ‘y(ield)ing fruits and flowers’ PalapuzpadA (BUH); pra-sU.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2, 4 A, utpad c., jan c. (janayati).<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 tyaj 1 P, ut-vi-sfj 6 P, hA 3 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 pra-dA, vi-tF 1 P, (with loc.).<BR>Ⓔv. i.ⒹvaSaM gam 1 P or yA-i 2 P, vaSIBU 1 P.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 SaraRaM prapad 4 A or gam &c.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		3 (to anotherʼs opinion) anu-man 4 A, nirbaMDaM-svAgrahaM-tyaj, anu-ruD 4 A; ‘y(ield) to a superior foe’ vEtasIM vfttiM ASri 1 U (R. iv. 35); ‘y(ield)ed to his prowess’ vikramaSAlinastasya vaSaM yayO; ‘does not y(ield) to Sachi in majestic splendour’ ojasvitayA na parihIyate SacyAH (V. 3).<BR>Ⓔs.ⒹutpannaM, PalaM, lABaH<BR>Ⓝ[Yield]ing,Ⓒa.ⒹPalada-prada-dAyin.<BR>Ⓑ<BR>		2 anuroDin, anuvartin, anukUla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AE&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

